    <bpmn:process id="W_W776" name="W776. Store-Level Product Recall Customer Notification Execution" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Product recall activated per W29; customer notification required
Frequency: Ad-hoc; ~2–4 product recalls per year requiring customer notification
Volume: Per recall: ~100–5,000 affected customer transactions depending on SKU velocity
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, CSR, LP Analyst, Customer, HQ Compliance
Source: workflow W776 — Store-Level Product Recall Customer Notification Execution</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W776_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W776_Lane1" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W776_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W776_Lane3" name="CSR">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W776_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W776_Start5" name="Product recall activated per W29; customer notification required">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W776_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W776_Task6" name="Recall notification receipt">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Recall notification receipt: Store Manager receives recall notification from HQ Compliance per W29: (a) affected SKU(s), (b) recall reason and risk level, (c) affected date range of sales, (d) required customer action (return, dispose, exchange), (e) customer notification template approved by Legal
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W776_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W776_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W776_Task7" name="Affected transaction identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Affected transaction identification: System queries POS transaction history per store for affected SKU within specified date range: (a) transaction date/time, (b) customer identification (loyalty member, trade account, or anonymous cash sale), (c) quantity purchased, (d) payment method for refund reference
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Automated + 15 min review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W776_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W776_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W776_Task8" name="Loyalty member notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Loyalty member notification: For identified loyalty members: (a) system sends notification via W708 (SMS, email, app push) using approved template, (b) notification includes: product description and image, recall reason, risk level, required action, return instructions, refund/exchange options, store contact number, (c) system tracks notification delivery status
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W776_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W776_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W776_Task9" name="Trade account notification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Trade account notification: For identified trade/B2B accounts: (a) Store Manager calls Key Account Manager for direct customer notification per W617, (b) notification logged in customer account per CRM, (c) return/exchange logistics coordinated (bulk pickup or store return)
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): Sales Manager
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W776_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W776_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W776_Task10" name="In-store recall signage">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: In-store recall signage: CSR posts recall notice at: (a) store entrance, (b) customer service counter, (c) product&#x27;s former shelf location (with &quot;RECALLED — Do Not Sell&quot; sign), (d) store social media pages; notice includes product image, recall reason, and action instructions
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W776_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W776_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W776_Task11" name="Customer return processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Customer return processing: Customers returning recalled products: (a) CSR processes return per W12 with special recall reason code, (b) no receipt required for recalled items, (c) full refund regardless of item condition (safety recall), (d) system flags return as recall-related for W627 effectiveness tracking
Responsible (R): CSR
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5-10 min/return</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W776_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W776_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W776_Task12" name="Daily recall status reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Daily recall status reporting: Store Manager reports daily to HQ Compliance: (a) customers notified vs. total affected, (b) returns received, (c) notification delivery failures, (d) customer inquiries or complaints about the recall
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15 min/day during recall</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W776_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W776_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W776_Task13" name="Recall close-out">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Recall close-out: When recall period ends per W627: (a) Store Manager confirms all customer notification attempts completed, (b) removes in-store recall signage, (c) files recall documentation per W256 retention policy, (d) submits final store-level recall effectiveness report
Responsible (R): Store Manager
Accountable (A): HQ Compliance
Duration: 30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W776_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W776_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W776_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W776_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W776_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
