    <bpmn:process id="W_W913" name="W913. Store-Level Emergency Generator Fuel Reserve Management &amp; DOE Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Daily fuel level monitoring; also triggered by PAGASA typhoon advisory (W576), rotational brownout schedule (W470), or fuel reorder point
Frequency: Daily monitoring; fuel delivery ~2–4 times/month per store; 200 stores × ~2–4 deliveries/month = ~400–800 fuel deliveries/month chain-wide
Volume: Average 500–1,000 liters diesel per store per month; 8-hour reserve = ~200–270 liters per store (at the 25–33 L/h rate)
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Store Manager, Stock Associate (fuel handling), Fuel Vendor, CIT (fuel delivery), Facilities Maintenance (generator service W808), Regional Manager (emergency escalation)
Source: workflow W913 — Store-Level Emergency Generator Fuel Reserve Management &amp; DOE Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W913_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W913_Lane1" name="Stock Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W913_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W913_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W913_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W913_Lane2" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W913_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W913_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W913_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W913_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W913_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W913_Start5" name="Daily fuel level monitoring; also triggered by PAGASA typhoon advisory (W576), rotational…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W913_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W913_Task6" name="Daily Fuel Level Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Daily Fuel Level Monitoring: (a) Stock Associate performs daily morning generator fuel level check using dipstick or digital gauge; (b) fuel level recorded in store operations mobile app with: current liters, generator run hours since last refuel, estimated remaining runtime at typical load (POS + CCTV + lighting + refrigeration = ~60–70% generator load = ~6–8 hours per 200 liters); (c) system compares current fuel level against minimum reserve threshold: Green (≥8-hour reserve), Amber (4–8 hour reserve), Red (&lt;4-hour reserve); (d) Amber: auto-generates fuel delivery order to contracted fuel vendor; (e) Red: urgent fuel delivery request + Store Manager notification + Regional Manager alert; (f) daily fuel data consolidated in store KPI dashboard per W665
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W913_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W913_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W913_Task7" name="Fuel Replenishment &amp; Delivery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fuel Replenishment &amp; Delivery: (a) standard replenishment: fuel vendor delivers diesel in 200-liter drums or via mini-tanker to store; (b) delivery scheduling: system auto-schedules delivery when fuel drops below Amber threshold; delivery within 24 hours (metro), 48 hours (provincial); (c) delivery receiving: Stock Associate verifies delivery quantity (dipstick reading before and after, or flow meter reading from tanker), checks fuel quality (visual inspection — no water contamination), and signs delivery receipt; (d) fuel storage: diesel stored in approved container(s) per DOE guidelines — properly labeled, ventilated area, away from ignition sources, with spill containment per W238 hazmat spill protocol; (e) delivery reconciliation: delivery receipt entered in system against PO; 3-way match per W7 for fuel vendor invoice; (f) emergency fuel procurement: if contracted vendor cannot deliver within SLA (e.g., during typhoon), Store Manager authorized to purchase from nearest fuel station using petty cash per W25 with receipt
Responsible (R): Stock Associate / Fuel Vendor / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 30–45 min per delivery</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W913_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W913_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W913_Task8" name="Typhoon Season Fuel Surge Protocol">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Typhoon Season Fuel Surge Protocol: (a) PAGASA Signal No. 1 advisory for store location (per W576): system triggers fuel surge order — additional 400 liters (total reserve: ~18–24 hours at the 6–8 h/200 L rate) above minimum; (b) fuel vendor pre-positions surge deliveries within 24 hours of Signal No. 1; (c) Signal No. 2: fuel reserve increased to 24-hour capacity (600–800 liters); (d) post-typhoon: extended outage areas receive priority fuel delivery coordination from Regional Manager; (e) fuel expense tracking during typhoon events for insurance claim documentation per W858 (business interruption claim requires proof of extra expenses incurred); (f) annual: pre-typhoon season (May) fuel vendor capacity confirmation and surge delivery SLA review
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Fuel Vendor / Regional Manager
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 30 min per event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W913_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W913_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W913_Task9" name="Generator Fuel Consumption &amp; Efficiency Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Generator Fuel Consumption &amp; Efficiency Monitoring: (a) system tracks: fuel consumption rate (liters/hour) per generator load level, total monthly fuel cost per store, generator runtime hours, and outage frequency/duration per store; (b) monthly: fuel consumption benchmarking across 200 stores (liters/month, liters/run-hour, cost/store); stores consuming &gt;20% above benchmark flagged for generator maintenance per W808 (dirty fuel filters, aging generators consume more fuel); (c) quarterly: fuel vendor performance review — delivery reliability, price competitiveness, fuel quality; fuel cost per store integrated into store operating budget per W489; (d) annual: generator fuel cost trend analysis and generator replacement ROI (new efficient generator vs. continued high fuel cost of aging unit) per W799 vehicle/equipment lifecycle logic
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager / Facilities Maintenance
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W913_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W913_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W913_Task10" name="DOE &amp; Environmental Compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: DOE &amp; Environmental Compliance: (a) DENR-EMB Permit to Operate (PTO) for standby generators per W477 (air-pollution source equipment under RA 8749/Clean Air Act IRR; DOE governs fuel, not equipment PTOs) maintained for each store with &gt;500 liters diesel storage; (b) fuel storage compliance: containers meet DOE safety standards (proper labeling, fire extinguisher within 5 meters, no smoking signage, spill containment); (c) emissions: generator exhaust emissions checked during quarterly maintenance per W808; DOE emission standards compliance; (d) fuel purchase records retained for 10 years per BIR/NIRC requirements (Sec. 235 as amended by TRAIN) (fuel expense for tax deduction per W590); (e) DENR spill contingency: minor spill (&lt;5 liters) — sand/absorbent cleanup per W238; major spill (&gt;5 liters) — DENR notification within 24 hours per W433; (f) annual: DOE compliance self-assessment integrated into W506 unified compliance calendar
Responsible (R): Store Manager / Facilities Maintenance
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 2–3 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W913_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W913_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W913_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W913_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W913_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: Store Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W913_Assoc13" sourceRef="W913_Annotation12" targetRef="W913_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
