    <bpmn:process id="W_W943" name="W943. Customer Glass Cutting &amp; Custom Flat Glass Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests custom-cut flat glass at the in-store glass cutting station or via ecommerce special order
Frequency: ~3,000–4,000 transactions/month chain-wide (~15–20/store/month)
Volume: 1–3 pieces per transaction; average 2 cuts per piece
Owner: Department Supervisor (Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate (Glass Specialist), Customer, Receiving Clerk (glass inventory handling), Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W943 — Customer Glass Cutting &amp; Custom Flat Glass Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W943_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W943_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W943_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W943_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W943_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W943_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W943_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W943_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W943_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W943_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W943_Start3" name="Customer requests custom-cut flat glass at the in-store glass cutting station or via…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W943_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W943_Task4" name="Customer Request &amp; Measurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Request &amp; Measurement: Customer approaches glass cutting station with dimensions or physical item (broken glass, window frame) for measurement; the Sales Associate (Glass Specialist) verifies glass type (clear 3mm/4mm/5mm/6mm, tinted, frosted, textured, mirror), dimensions (max 1.22m × 2.44m standard sheet), edge finish (plain cut, polished, beveled), and quantity; for walk-in: Sales Associate measures physical item with steel tape; for ecommerce: customer provides dimensions via online order form (W949 visualizer integration for photo-to-dimension estimation)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W943_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W943_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W943_Task5" name="Feasibility Check &amp; Quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Feasibility Check &amp; Quotation: Sales Associate confirms: (a) glass type availability at store — system checks real-time stock per W533; if unavailable, Sales Associate checks nearest store (W22 transfer) or DC replenishment lead time; (b) dimensional feasibility — maximum cut size, minimum cut size (10cm × 10cm), tolerances (±2mm manual, ±1mm CNC); (c) safety compliance — tempered glass required for shower enclosures, large panels &gt; 0.5sqm per National Building Code; tempered glass outsourced to accredited fabricator per W600 with 3–5 day lead time; (d) system generates quotation: glass material cost (per sqm) + cutting fee (per cut) + edge finish surcharge (per linear meter) + optional delivery fee; quotation valid for 7 days
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W943_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W943_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W943_Task6" name="Order Acceptance &amp; Payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Order Acceptance &amp; Payment: Customer accepts quotation; Sales Associate creates service work order (SWO) in POS system per W544; customer pays at POS — material cost + cutting fee + edge finish + associated products (sealant, clips, moulding) in single transaction; POS prints SWO receipt with: order number, glass specifications, dimensions, edge finish, promised ready time, and customer copy; system allocates glass sheet from inventory and creates cutting instruction for the Sales Associate (Glass Specialist)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Cashier
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W943_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W943_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W943_Task7" name="Glass Cutting Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Glass Cutting Execution: The Sales Associate (Glass Specialist) retrieves glass sheet from storage rack (backroom glass storage area, vertical rack with dividers by type/thickness); the Sales Associate (Glass Specialist) dons PPE per W140 (cut-resistant gloves, safety goggles, closed-toe shoes); performs cuts using manual glass cutter (score-and-snap for straight cuts) or CNC glass cutting table (available at top 30 stores); applies edge finish: plain cut (default), polished edge (hand polisher), or beveled edge (beveling machine — top 30 stores); measures finished piece against order dimensions; records cut dimensions and waste factor on SWO
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Glass Specialist)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–25 min/piece</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W943_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W943_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W943_Task8" name="Quality Inspection &amp; Customer Handover">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quality Inspection &amp; Customer Handover: The Sales Associate (Glass Specialist) inspects: (a) dimensional accuracy (±2mm tolerance); (b) edge quality (no chips, cracks, burrs); (c) glass type and thickness match to order; failed inspection → recut from new sheet, waste piece dispositioned per W91; wraps finished piece in protective packing material (bubble wrap or corrugated sheet); customer inspects and signs acceptance on SWO; system closes SWO and posts sale; system updates inventory: glass sheet consumed + waste factor (average 10–15% waste per sheet) posted to scrap per W443
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W943_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W943_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W943_Task9" name="Daily Station Cleanup &amp; Waste Disposal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Daily Station Cleanup &amp; Waste Disposal: At end of day: The Sales Associate (Glass Specialist) cleans glass cutting station; collects glass waste (offcuts, broken pieces) in designated sharps/glass waste container; waste glass disposed per W82 hazardous/non-hazardous waste protocol (flat glass is non-hazardous but requires special handling for sharp edges); system records daily glass waste volume for inventory reconciliation; glass cutting tools inspected and maintained (cutter wheel replacement every 200 linear meters of cut)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Glass Specialist)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W943_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W943_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W943_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W943_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W943_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: PPE enforcement, first aid kit proximity per W501, and incident reporting per W140 mitigate
Owner: Department Supervisor (Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W943_Assoc12" sourceRef="W943_Annotation11" targetRef="W943_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
