    <bpmn:process id="W_W944" name="W944. Customer Pipe Threading, Cutting &amp; Fabrication Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests custom-cut or threaded pipe at the in-store pipe fabrication station or via ecommerce special order
Frequency: ~4,000–6,000 transactions/month chain-wide (~20–30/store/month)
Volume: 1–5 pieces per transaction; average 2 cuts + 1 thread per transaction
Owner: Department Supervisor (Plumbing/Electrical)
Participants: Sales Associate (Pipe Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (pricing), vendor (special alloy sourcing)
Source: workflow W944 — Customer Pipe Threading, Cutting &amp; Fabrication Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W944_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W944_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W944_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W944_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W944_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W944_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W944_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W944_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W944_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W944_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W944_Start3" name="Customer requests custom-cut or threaded pipe at the in-store pipe fabrication station or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W944_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W944_Task4" name="Customer Request &amp; Specification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Request &amp; Specification: Customer provides pipe specification: (a) pipe type — GI (galvanized iron), black iron, stainless steel, copper, or PVC; (b) nominal diameter — ½&quot; to 4&quot; for GI/black iron; ¼&quot; to 2&quot; for copper; PVC cut only (no threading); (c) cut lengths — specific lengths in cm; (d) thread requirements — both ends, one end, or no threads; (e) thread type — BSPT (standard in Philippines) or NPT; Sales Associate verifies specifications and selects appropriate pipe from inventory
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W944_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W944_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W944_Task5" name="Feasibility Check &amp; Quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Feasibility Check &amp; Quotation: Sales Associate confirms: (a) pipe type and diameter availability at store — system checks real-time stock per W533; (b) cutting feasibility — pipe cutter capacity (manual for ≤ 2&quot;, power cutter for 2½&quot;–4&quot;); (c) threading feasibility — pipe threading machine capacity (½&quot;–4&quot; BSPT); (d) minimum piece length — 5cm for cuts, 3cm minimum threaded section; (e) system generates quotation: pipe material cost (charged per standard length consumed, not per cut piece) + cutting fee (per cut) + threading fee (per end) + optional delivery; customer informed that leftover pipe pieces are customer&#x27;s property per standard practice
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W944_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W944_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W944_Task6" name="Order Acceptance &amp; Payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Order Acceptance &amp; Payment: Customer accepts quotation; Sales Associate creates SWO in POS per W544; customer pays at POS; POS prints SWO receipt with: order number, pipe specifications, cut lengths, thread details, promised ready time; system allocates pipe from inventory; for large orders (≥10 pieces or ≥4&quot; diameter): Sales Associate schedules pickup time within 2 hours to avoid station congestion
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Cashier
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W944_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W944_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W944_Task7" name="Pipe Cutting &amp; Threading Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Pipe Cutting &amp; Threading Execution: The Sales Associate (Pipe Specialist) retrieves pipe from storage rack; dons PPE per W140 (safety goggles, cut-resistant gloves, steel-toe boots, ear protection for power cutting); measures and marks cut points with measuring tape and marker; performs cuts: (a) PVC — manual PVC cutter (quick, clean cut); (b) GI/copper ≤ 2&quot; — manual pipe cutter (rotating blade); (c) GI/black iron 2½&quot;–4&quot; — power pipe cutter (abrasive chop saw); deburrs cut ends with file or deburring tool; for threaded ends: mounts pipe in pipe threading machine (½&quot;–4&quot; capacity), applies cutting oil, threads to BSPT standard (11 threads per inch for ½&quot;–¾&quot;, taper per BS 21); cleans threaded ends (removes metal chips, applies anti-rust coating for GI); measures finished pieces against order
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Pipe Specialist)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–20 min/piece</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W944_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W944_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W944_Task8" name="Quality Inspection &amp; Customer Handover">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quality Inspection &amp; Customer Handover: The Sales Associate (Pipe Specialist) inspects: (a) cut length accuracy (±3mm); (b) thread quality — thread gauge fit check (go/no-go gauge for BSPT threads); (c) deburr quality — no sharp edges; (d) anti-rust coating applied (GI only); customer inspects and signs acceptance on SWO; system closes SWO; leftover pipe pieces offered to customer or disposed per W91 if customer declines
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W944_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W944_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W944_Task9" name="Weekly Machine Maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Weekly Machine Maintenance: Pipe threading machine: weekly oil level check, die head cleaning, blade inspection; pipe cutter: blade replacement every 500 cuts; maintenance logged in Oracle eAM (fit-gap F5) per W650; consumable tracking: cutting oil, deburring tools, anti-rust spray replenished from store inventory
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Pipe Specialist)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W944_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W944_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W944_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W944_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W944_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Department Supervisor (Plumbing/Electrical)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
