    <bpmn:process id="W_W946" name="W946. Customer Screen Door &amp; Window Screen Custom Fabrication Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests custom-fabricated screen door or window screen at the in-store service counter or via ecommerce
Frequency: ~1,500–2,500 transactions/month chain-wide (~8–12/store/month)
Volume: 1–3 screens per transaction
Owner: Department Supervisor (Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate (Fabrication Specialist), Customer, Category Manager (screen material pricing)
Source: workflow W946 — Customer Screen Door &amp; Window Screen Custom Fabrication Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W946_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W946_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W946_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W946_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W946_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W946_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W946_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W946_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W946_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W946_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W946_Start3" name="Customer requests custom-fabricated screen door or window screen at the in-store service…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W946_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W946_Task4" name="Customer Request &amp; Measurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Request &amp; Measurement: Customer provides window or door opening dimensions (width × height), or brings old/damaged screen for replication; Sales Associate records: (a) frame material — aluminum (standard) or wood (premium); (b) frame profile — standard flat, decorative, or retractable; (c) mesh type — fiberglass (standard, 18×16 mesh), stainless steel (security screen, 12×12 mesh), or pet-resistant (heavy-duty fiberglass); (d) mesh color — charcoal (standard), gray, or silver; (e) frame color — white, brown, bronze, or natural aluminum; (f) hardware — hinge type (butt hinge, piano hinge), handle type, latch/lock type; (g) installation type — surface mount or recessed; Sales Associate independently measures customer-provided physical items for verification
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W946_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W946_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W946_Task5" name="Quotation &amp; Order Acceptance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Quotation &amp; Order Acceptance: System generates quotation: (a) frame material cost (per linear meter of aluminum/wood profile); (b) mesh material cost (per sqm); (c) hardware kit (hinges, handle, latch); (d) fabrication labor fee (per screen, based on size); (e) optional installation fee (outsourced per W138, only for BuildRight service area); customer accepts; Sales Associate creates SWO per W544; customer pays material deposit (50%) with balance due at pickup; system allocates materials from inventory
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Cashier
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W946_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W946_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W946_Task6" name="Frame Cutting &amp; Assembly">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Frame Cutting &amp; Assembly: The Sales Associate (Fabrication Specialist) retrieves aluminum profile stock or wood stock; cuts frame pieces to dimensions using miter saw (aluminum) or table saw (wood) at 45° corners; for aluminum: joins corners with aluminum corner keys and crimping tool; for wood: joins with wood glue, dowels, and corner braces; dry-fits frame to verify dimensions
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Fabrication Specialist)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 20–30 min/screen</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W946_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W946_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W946_Task7" name="Mesh Installation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Mesh Installation: The Sales Associate (Fabrication Specialist) cuts mesh to frame dimensions plus 2cm overhang on all sides; lays mesh over frame with groove facing up; presses rubber spline into groove over mesh using spline roller tool, starting from one corner and working around; trims excess mesh with utility knife; inspects mesh tension (uniform, no wrinkles, no gaps) and spline seating (fully seated in groove, no protrusion)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Fabrication Specialist)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min/screen</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W946_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W946_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W946_Task8" name="Hardware Installation &amp; Quality Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Hardware Installation &amp; Quality Check: The Sales Associate (Fabrication Specialist) installs hinges (2–3 per screen depending on size), handle, and latch/lock per customer specification; quality check: (a) frame squareness (diagonal measurement within ±3mm); (b) mesh tension and uniformity; (c) hardware alignment and operation; (d) overall dimensions match order (±3mm tolerance); marks BuildRight label on frame (date, store, order number)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Fabrication Specialist)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min/screen</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W946_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W946_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W946_Task9" name="Customer Pickup &amp; Final Payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Customer Pickup &amp; Final Payment: Customer picks up completed screen(s) within 7 days of notification; inspects and verifies fit against physical opening (or Customer Service Counter assists with measurement verification); customer pays remaining balance at POS; system closes SWO; if customer requests delivery, W668 delivery coordination triggered
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Cashier
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W946_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W946_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W946_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W946_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W946_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Department Supervisor (Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W946_Assoc12" sourceRef="W946_Annotation11" targetRef="W946_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W946_Flow13" sourceRef="W946_Start3" targetRef="W946_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W946_Flow14" sourceRef="W946_Task4" targetRef="W946_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W946_Flow15" sourceRef="W946_Task5" targetRef="W946_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W946_Flow16" sourceRef="W946_Task6" targetRef="W946_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W946_Flow17" sourceRef="W946_Task7" targetRef="W946_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W946_Flow18" sourceRef="W946_Task8" targetRef="W946_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W946_Flow19" sourceRef="W946_Task9" targetRef="W946_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W946_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W946_plane" bpmnElement="W_W946">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W946_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W946_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
