    <bpmn:process id="W_W953" name="W953. Customer Contractor Micro-Lending Partnership Program Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Trade/B2B customer requests short-term financing for materials purchase, or lending partner submits loan application derived from BuildRight purchase history
Frequency: ~500–800 loan applications/month; ~70% approval rate
Volume: PHP 10,000–500,000 per loan; average PHP 80,000
Owner: Head of Trade / Account Management
Participants: Customer (Contractor/Trade), Lending Partner (accredited microfinance institution/bank), Trade Sales Representative, Finance (AR), Legal
Source: workflow W953 — Customer Contractor Micro-Lending Partnership Program Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W953_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W953_Lane1" name="Trade Sales Rep">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W953_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W953_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W953_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W953_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W953_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W953_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W953_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W953_Lane4" name="Head of Trade">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W953_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W953_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W953_Start6" name="Trade/B2B customer requests short-term financing for materials purchase, or lending…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W953_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W953_Task7" name="Customer Enrollment &amp; Consent">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Enrollment &amp; Consent: Trade customer enrolls in the micro-lending program: (a) Trade Sales Representative explains program — BuildRight partners with [accredited lenders], customer applies for short-term financing through the partner, BuildRight shares verified purchase data (with consent) to support credit assessment, BuildRight does NOT guarantee or co-sign loans; (b) customer signs consent form per RA 10173 authorizing BuildRight to share purchase history and payment behavior data with accredited lending partners; (c) consent captured in ERP with revocable option; (d) customer selects preferred lending partner from accredited list (2–3 partners per region)
Responsible (R): Trade Sales Rep / Customer
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W953_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W953_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W953_Task8" name="Loan Application &amp; Data Sharing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Loan Application &amp; Data Sharing: Customer applies for loan: (a) via BuildRight mobile app — customer selects loan amount and term, system auto-populates application with verified BuildRight purchase data (12-month purchase history, average monthly spend, payment timeliness, active trade account standing); (b) via lending partner directly — customer references BuildRight trade account number; lending partner requests data share via API; system validates customer consent and transmits authorized data; (c) lending partner performs independent credit assessment using: shared BuildRight data + partner&#x27;s own credit scoring + other data sources; BuildRight does NOT influence lending decisions
Responsible (R): Customer / System / Lending Partner
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 10–15 min (customer side); automated data sharing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W953_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W953_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W953_Task9" name="Loan Disbursement &amp; Material Purchase">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Loan Disbursement &amp; Material Purchase: Lending partner approves loan and disburses: (a) directly to customer&#x27;s bank account or e-wallet; (b) customer purchases materials from BuildRight using: (i) cash/card payment with loan proceeds; (ii) lending partner&#x27;s virtual card (if partner offers co-branded card); (iii) BuildRight trade account (W24) with loan proceeds used to pay trade balance; system tracks loan-funded purchases for program analytics; customer is NOT required to spend loan proceeds at BuildRight (no tie-in per BSP regulations), but BuildRight expects high share-of-wallet based on convenience and loyalty
Responsible (R): Customer / System / Lending Partner
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management
Duration: 5–10 min (purchase)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W953_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W953_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W953_Task10" name="Repayment Monitoring &amp; Data Refresh">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Repayment Monitoring &amp; Data Refresh: (a) lending partner manages loan repayment independently — customer repays lending partner per agreed terms; (b) BuildRight receives monthly anonymized portfolio data from lending partners: approval rate, average loan size, default rate, repayment performance; (c) BuildRight refreshes customer&#x27;s shared data monthly: updated purchase history and payment behavior transmitted to lending partners for ongoing credit assessment; (d) if customer&#x27;s BuildRight trade account goes on credit hold per W888, lending partner is notified (per consent agreement) as a risk indicator
Responsible (R): System / Lending Partner
Accountable (A): Head of Trade / Account Management / CFO
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W953_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W953_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W953_Task11" name="Program Governance &amp; Partner Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Program Governance &amp; Partner Management: (a) quarterly: Head of Trade / Account Management reviews program metrics — enrollment count, application volume, approval rate, default rate, average loan size, BuildRight revenue impact, referral fee income; (b) semi-annually: Legal reviews lending partner compliance with BSP regulations, the Truth in Lending Act (RA 3765), and data privacy (RA 10173); (c) annually: lending partner accreditation renewal per W36 vendor onboarding framework; partner performance scorecard: approval rate, customer satisfaction, default rate, complaint resolution; (d) referral fee reconciliation: Finance verifies lending partner referral fee payments against loan disbursement records
Responsible (R): Head of Trade / Account Management / Legal / Finance
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Quarterly review + annual renewal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W953_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W953_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W953_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W953_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W953_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: per step 1
Owner: Head of Trade / Account Management</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W953_Assoc14" sourceRef="W953_Annotation13" targetRef="W953_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W953_Flow15" sourceRef="W953_Start6" targetRef="W953_Task7" />
