    <bpmn:process id="W_W955" name="W955. Customer Daily-Wage Construction Worker Hiring Facilitation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests assistance finding daily-wage construction workers, or workers register at BuildRight for daily work availability
Frequency: ~8,000–12,000 hiring facilitations/month chain-wide (~40–60/store/month)
Volume: 1–5 workers per hiring request
Owner: Store Manager
Participants: Customer, Construction Worker (applicant), Customer Service Representative, Store Manager
Source: workflow W955 — Customer Daily-Wage Construction Worker Hiring Facilitation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W955_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W955_Lane1" name="Customer Service Rep">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W955_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W955_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W955_Lane2" name="Worker">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W955_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W955_Lane3" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W955_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W955_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W955_Lane4" name="Store Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W955_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W955_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W955_Start6" name="Customer requests assistance finding daily-wage construction workers, or workers register…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W955_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W955_Task7" name="Worker Registration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Worker Registration: Construction worker visits BuildRight customer service counter to register: (a) provides: full name, mobile number, barangay/address, trade/skill (carpenter, mason, plumber, electrician, painter, tile setter, laborer/handyman, welder), years of experience, daily rate expectation, availability (Mon–Sat selection), and preferred BuildRight store; (b) Customer Service Representative verifies: valid government ID (presented and visually verified — PhilHealth, barangay clearance, voter&#x27;s ID, or any valid ID); (c) system creates worker profile — NOT an employee record, but a facilitation directory entry; (d) worker receives BuildRight loyalty card enrollment per W551 (optional but encouraged — tracks store visits for activity-based availability status); (e) worker receives printed registration card with BuildRight registration ID; (f) worker profile active for 90 days, renewable with re-verification; (g) registration is FREE — no fee to worker or customer
Responsible (R): Customer Service Rep / Worker
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min/worker</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W955_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W955_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W955_Task8" name="Worker Availability Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Worker Availability Management: Registered workers maintain availability: (a) active status: worker checks in at store kiosk or via SMS/App each morning by 7:00 AM to signal availability for the day; (b) if worker does not check in for 3 consecutive working days, system marks profile &quot;Inactive — last checked in [date]&quot;; (c) worker can deactivate profile anytime (found long-term employment, traveling, etc.); (d) system purges profiles inactive &gt; 90 days — worker must re-register; (e) worker can update: daily rate, skills, and contact number at any time via kiosk or app
Responsible (R): Worker / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1 min/day (worker check-in)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W955_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W955_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W955_Task9" name="Customer Hiring Request">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Customer Hiring Request: Customer browses available workers: (a) in-store: dedicated kiosk (W924) displays today&#x27;s available workers by trade, daily rate, and years of experience; no names or photos displayed until customer selects — only trade, rate range, experience, and registration ID; (b) mobile app: same directory with distance filter (workers registered at nearby stores); (c) customer selects worker(s) and requests contact information; system sends worker&#x27;s mobile number to customer via SMS (with worker&#x27;s consent per registration terms); (d) alternatively: customer posts a job request at the kiosk (trade needed, number of workers, date, location, offered daily rate) and available workers see the posting at the store kiosk; (e) BuildRight does NOT negotiate rates, verify worker quality, or guarantee workmanship
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W955_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W955_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W955_Task10" name="Hiring Confirmation &amp; Feedback">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Hiring Confirmation &amp; Feedback: After hiring: (a) customer optionally reports hiring outcome via app or SMS: &quot;hired,&quot; &quot;no-show,&quot; &quot;unsatisfactory&quot;; (b) worker optionally reports: &quot;hired,&quot; &quot;customer did not show,&quot; &quot;unsafe conditions&quot;; (c) system tracks: hiring frequency per worker, no-show rate, customer feedback (positive/negative/no report); (d) workers with &gt; 3 customer &quot;no-show&quot; reports in 30 days are flagged for Store Manager review — may be suspended from directory; (e) workers with consistently positive feedback receive &quot;Recommended&quot; badge in directory (based on ≥ 5 positive reports, no negative reports in 90 days); (f) customers with &gt; 3 worker &quot;no-show-for-customer&quot; reports are flagged — workers can see customer rating before accepting
Responsible (R): Customer / Worker / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 2–3 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W955_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W955_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W955_Task11" name="Program Governance &amp; Compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Program Governance &amp; Compliance: (a) Store Manager reviews worker directory weekly: new registrations, active counts, flagged workers, customer complaints; (b) quarterly: HR reviews program for DOLE compliance — BuildRight is a facilitation/directory service, NOT an employer or contractor; workers are NOT BuildRight employees; no co-employment risk per DOLE DO 174 analysis; (c) annual: Legal reviews terms of service and liability disclaimers; workers sign acknowledgement that BuildRight is not their employer; customers acknowledge BuildRight does not guarantee worker quality; (d) if worker or customer reports safety incident: Store Manager logs per W140 and advises both parties of their independent responsibilities
Responsible (R): Store Manager / HR / Legal
Accountable (A): COO / VP Legal
Duration: 1–2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W955_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W955_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W955_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W955_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W955_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: facilitation-only terms with legal review per Step 5c (no co-employment); operational: government-ID verification at registration (Step 1b); operational: feedback-driven directory governance with Store Manager review (Steps 4d/5a)
Owner: Store Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W955_Assoc14" sourceRef="W955_Annotation13" targetRef="W955_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
