    <bpmn:process id="W_W960" name="W960. Seasonal Forward Stock Pre-Positioning &amp; Regional Buffer Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Seasonal demand forecast indicates upcoming spike requiring pre-positioned buffer stock at regional hubs (DCs and forward locations)
Frequency: 4–6 pre-positioning events/year (aligned with Philippine seasonal calendar: rainy season, summer, Christmas, back-to-school)
Volume: 50–200 SKUs per event; buffer stock value PHP 50–200M per event
Owner: Supply Chain Planning Manager
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Category Manager, DC Manager, Finance (working capital), Procurement, Transport Manager
Source: workflow W960 — Seasonal Forward Stock Pre-Positioning &amp; Regional Buffer Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W960_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W960_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W960_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W960_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W960_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W960_Lane2" name="Finance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W960_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W960_Lane3" name="DC Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W960_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W960_Lane4" name="Supply Chain Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W960_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W960_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W960_Start6" name="Seasonal demand forecast indicates upcoming spike requiring pre-positioned buffer stock…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W960_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W960_Task7" name="Seasonal Demand Forecast &amp; Buffer Quantification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Seasonal Demand Forecast &amp; Buffer Quantification: (a) Merchandise Planner runs seasonal demand model per W31 using: (i) historical seasonal sales (3-year rolling); (ii) weather forecast (PAGASA seasonal outlook); (iii) typhoon probability models for island regions; (iv) planned promotions per W13 calendar; (v) macroeconomic factors (remittance inflows for OFW construction projects, election-related construction spending); (b) Supply Chain Planning Manager quantifies buffer stock requirements per SKU per DC: buffer = (forecasted peak month demand × 1.5 safety factor) − (regular replenishment capacity during peak); (c) buffer stock segmented by: (i) guaranteed sellers (seasonal staples — cement, plywood, waterproofing, paint, nails — minimal markdown risk); (ii) seasonal specifics (Christmas lights, garden tools — higher markdown risk if unsold); (iii) emergency response items (tarpaulins, rope, flashlights — critical for post-typhoon demand, minimal markdown risk as items are evergreen)
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Supply Chain Manager
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 8–12 hours/event</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W960_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W960_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W960_Task8" name="Working Capital Approval &amp; Procurement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Working Capital Approval &amp; Procurement: (a) Finance reviews buffer stock investment: total buffer value, incremental carrying cost, and cash flow impact per W233; (b) tiered approval: (i) buffer value ≤ PHP 20M → VP Supply Chain approves; (ii) PHP 20–50M → COO approves; (iii) &gt; PHP 50M → CEO approves; (c) Procurement executes seasonal buy orders per W2: (i) import orders (45–90 day lead time) placed 3–4 months before season; (ii) local orders placed 4–6 weeks before season; (iii) blanket PO releases (W2C) for guaranteed sellers with vendor volume commitment; (d) vendor delivery scheduled to arrive at DC 2–4 weeks before projected demand start
Responsible (R): Finance / Procurement
Accountable (A): COO / CEO
Duration: 4–8 hours (procurement)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W960_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W960_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W960_Task9" name="Buffer Stock Receipt &amp; Pre-Positioning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Buffer Stock Receipt &amp; Pre-Positioning: (a) DC receives seasonal buffer stock per W3; (b) DC Manager allocates storage: (i) dedicated seasonal buffer zone in DC (physically separated from regular stock for tracking); (ii) for island-region stores (Visayas, Mindanao provincial): Merchandise Planner arranges forward staging — pre-ship buffer to key stores or rented forward warehouse locations 2 weeks before season; (iii) buffer stock tagged in WMS with &quot;SEASONAL BUFFER&quot; status — not available for regular replenishment until season start date; (iv) buffer stock tracked separately in inventory module for cost and sell-through analysis
Responsible (R): DC Manager / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Supply Chain Manager
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W960_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W960_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W960_Task10" name="In-Season Buffer Release &amp; Monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: In-Season Buffer Release &amp; Monitoring: (a) at season start date: system releases buffer stock for replenishment allocation; (b) weekly monitoring during season: (i) actual demand vs. forecast by SKU by region; (ii) buffer stock consumption rate; (iii) stockout risk assessment for fast-depleting buffers; (c) if demand exceeds forecast by &gt; 20%: Supply Chain Manager triggers emergency procurement per W60 for top-selling items; (d) if demand trails forecast by &gt; 20% at mid-season: Merchandise Planner adjusts replenishment to slow buffer consumption and begins planning post-season drawdown
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Manager / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 hours/week during season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W960_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W960_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W960_Task11" name="Post-Season Buffer Drawdown &amp; Disposition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-Season Buffer Drawdown &amp; Disposition: At season end: (a) Merchandise Planner generates buffer drawdown report: (i) remaining buffer stock by SKU and location; (ii) classification: evergreen items (can be sold year-round — cement, nails, tools), seasonal-only items (Christmas lights, flood control), and perishable/degrading items (paint with shelf life); (b) disposition per classification: (i) evergreen items: released to regular inventory pool; no markdown needed; (ii) seasonal-only items: markdown per W93 (clearance) if not sold within 30 days post-season; (iii) last season&#x27;s seasonal items: bulk liquidation or vendor return per W901 seasonal buy-back; (c) Finance calculates seasonal buffer ROI: (incremental gross margin from buffer sales + stockout avoidance value) − (incremental carrying cost + markdown cost + working capital opportunity cost); (d) lessons learned feed into next season&#x27;s planning per W32
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / Category Manager / Finance
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain / CFO
Duration: 4–6 hours/post-season</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W960_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W960_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W960_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W960_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W960_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: Supply Chain Planning Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Supply Chain Planning Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W960_Assoc14" sourceRef="W960_Annotation13" targetRef="W960_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W960_Flow15" sourceRef="W960_Start6" targetRef="W960_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W960_Flow16" sourceRef="W960_Task7" targetRef="W960_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W960_Flow17" sourceRef="W960_Task8" targetRef="W960_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W960_Flow18" sourceRef="W960_Task9" targetRef="W960_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W960_Flow19" sourceRef="W960_Task10" targetRef="W960_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W960_Flow20" sourceRef="W960_Task11" targetRef="W960_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W960_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W960_plane" bpmnElement="W_W960">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W960_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W960_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
