    <bpmn:process id="W_W986" name="W986. Store-Level Customer Rebar Cutting, Bending &amp; Fabrication Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer (contractor, builder, or homeowner) requests rebar cutting, bending, or custom fabrication at store
Frequency: ~5,000–7,000 transactions/month chain-wide (~25–35/store/month)
Volume: Average 50–200 pieces per transaction; 1–3 bar sizes per order
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate (Steel Specialist), Customer, Receiving Clerk (steel inventory), Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W986 — Store-Level Customer Rebar Cutting, Bending &amp; Fabrication Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W986_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W986_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W986_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W986_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W986_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W986_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W986_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W986_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W986_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W986_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W986_Start3" name="Customer (contractor, builder, or homeowner) requests rebar cutting, bending, or custom…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W986_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W986_Task4" name="Customer Order Intake &amp; Specification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Order Intake &amp; Specification: Customer provides rebar specifications: (a) rebar size (10mm, 12mm, 16mm, 20mm, 25mm) and grade (Grade 33, Grade 40, Grade 60); (b) cut lengths — specify number of pieces and length per piece (in cm or inches); (c) bend requirements — hook (90° or 180°, standard hook length = 6× bar diameter), L-bend (specify angle and leg lengths), U-shape (specify width and leg lengths), stirrup (specify dimensions for rectangular/ square ties); (d) quantity per specification; (e) reference to structural plan if available (Sales Associate can interpret simple rebar schedules); Sales Associate creates service work order (SWO) per W544
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W986_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W986_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W986_Task5" name="Feasibility Check &amp; Quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Feasibility Check &amp; Quotation: Sales Associate confirms: (a) rebar size availability — system checks real-time inventory per store; (b) bending feasibility — minimum bend radius = 3× bar diameter for Grade 33, 4× bar diameter for Grade 60 (PH structural engineering standard per NSCP); tight bends risk bar fracture; (c) maximum pieces per order — store capacity: ~200 pieces/hour for cutting only, ~100 pieces/hour for cutting + bending; (d) system generates quotation: rebar material cost (per piece at standard 6m length) + cutting fee (per cut) + bending fee (per bend) + waste factor (offcuts &lt;1m are scrap per W443); quotation valid for 3 days
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W986_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W986_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W986_Task6" name="Order Acceptance &amp; Payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Order Acceptance &amp; Payment: Customer accepts quotation; Sales Associate processes payment at POS — material cost + cutting fee + bending fee in single transaction; POS prints SWO receipt with: order number, rebar specifications, cut/bend details, promised ready time (standard: 2–4 hours for orders ≤100 pieces; next day for larger orders); system allocates rebar from inventory and creates fabrication instruction for the Sales Associate (Steel Specialist)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Cashier
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W986_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W986_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W986_Task7" name="Rebar Cutting &amp; Bending Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Rebar Cutting &amp; Bending Execution: The Sales Associate (Steel Specialist) retrieves rebar from yard storage per W3B; dons PPE per W140 (cut-resistant gloves, safety goggles, steel-toe boots, hard hat); performs operations: (a) cutting — uses hydraulic rebar cutter (capacity: up to 25mm); cuts to specified lengths with ±5mm tolerance; (b) bending — uses hydraulic rebar bender (capacity: up to 25mm); bends to specified angles and dimensions with ±3° angular tolerance; (c) sorts and bundles finished pieces by specification with tie wire; (d) tags each bundle with SWO number and customer name; (e) records waste offcuts — pieces &lt;1m dispositioned to scrap per W443; (f) for orders exceeding same-day capacity: queues remaining work for next morning and notifies customer of pickup time
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Steel Specialist)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–45 min (depends on order size)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W986_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W986_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W986_Task8" name="Quality Inspection &amp; Customer Handover">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quality Inspection &amp; Customer Handover: The Sales Associate (Steel Specialist) inspects: (a) dimensional accuracy — lengths ±5mm, bend angles ±3°; (b) bar integrity — no cracks, kinks, or excessive deformation at bends; (c) quantity per specification; failed inspection → re-cut/re-bend from new bar, waste piece to scrap; customer inspects finished pieces and signs acceptance on SWO; system closes SWO and posts sale; customer loads rebar at yard loading zone per W438; vehicle loading assistance per W950 provided for heavy orders
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W986_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W986_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W986_Task9" name="Daily Station Cleanup &amp; Waste Disposal">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Daily Station Cleanup &amp; Waste Disposal: At end of day: The Sales Associate (Steel Specialist) cleans rebar cutting/bending station; applies rust preventive to cutter and bender blades; collects steel offcuts in scrap bin; steel scrap sold to recycler per W443 (salvage monetization); system records daily scrap weight for inventory reconciliation; rebar fabrication tools inspected — hydraulic fluid levels, blade sharpness, bender pin condition
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Steel Specialist)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W986_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W986_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W986_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W986_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W986_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: PPE enforcement, equipment guard maintenance, and incident reporting per W140; operational: must optimize cutting sequence to minimize waste (nesting algorithm); operational: queue management with SMS notification when the order is ready
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W986_Assoc12" sourceRef="W986_Annotation11" targetRef="W986_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W986_Flow13" sourceRef="W986_Start3" targetRef="W986_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W986_Flow14" sourceRef="W986_Task4" targetRef="W986_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W986_Flow15" sourceRef="W986_Task5" targetRef="W986_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W986_Flow16" sourceRef="W986_Task6" targetRef="W986_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W986_Flow17" sourceRef="W986_Task7" targetRef="W986_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W986_Flow18" sourceRef="W986_Task8" targetRef="W986_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W986_Flow19" sourceRef="W986_Task9" targetRef="W986_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
