    <bpmn:process id="W_W988" name="W988. Store-Level Customer Welding &amp; Custom Metal Fabrication Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests custom metal fabrication or welding service at store
Frequency: ~2,500–3,500 transactions/month chain-wide (~12–17/store/month)
Volume: 1–5 pieces per transaction; average 2.3 pieces
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate (Welder/Fabricator), Customer, Category Manager (pricing)
Source: workflow W988 — Store-Level Customer Welding &amp; Custom Metal Fabrication Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W988_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W988_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W988_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W988_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W988_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W988_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W988_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W988_Lane2" name="Sales Associate (Welder">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W988_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W988_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W988_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W988_Start4" name="Customer requests custom metal fabrication or welding service at store">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W988_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W988_Task5" name="Customer Request &amp; Specification Intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Request &amp; Specification Intake: Customer provides fabrication requirements: (a) item description (gate, window grill, railing, frame, bracket, etc.); (b) dimensions — overall width, height, depth; member sizes and spacing; (c) material type — mild steel round tube (1&quot;, 1½&quot;, 2&quot;), square tube (1&quot;, 1½&quot;, 2&quot;), flat bar (⅜&quot;, ½&quot;, ¾&quot;), angle bar (1&quot;, 1¼&quot;, 1½&quot;), solid round bar, steel plate; (d) design — customer sketch, photograph of similar item, reference to existing structure, or description; (e) finish — raw steel (customer paints), primer only, primer + paint (BuildRight paints); (f) quantity; (g) any reference drawing or photo
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W988_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W988_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W988_Task6" name="Feasibility Check &amp; Quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Feasibility Check &amp; Quotation: Sales Associate confirms: (a) material availability — system checks real-time inventory per store; (b) fabrication complexity — simple (straight cuts, basic welds) vs. moderate (curves, patterns, ornamental) vs. complex (structural load-bearing, multi-component assemblies); (c) equipment capability — MIG welder (up to 6mm mild steel), angle grinder (cutting and finishing), drill press (hole drilling); stores do not perform CNC plasma cutting or heavy structural fabrication (those are referred to external fabricators); (d) estimated fabrication time — simple items: 1–3 hours; moderate: 3–8 hours; complex: 1–3 days; (e) system generates quotation: material cost (raw steel per length/piece) + fabrication fee (per hour or per piece based on complexity) + finish fee (primer/paint per sqm) + consumables (welding wire, gas, grinding discs); quotation valid for 7 days
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W988_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W988_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W988_Task7" name="Order Acceptance &amp; Payment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Order Acceptance &amp; Payment: Customer accepts quotation; Sales Associate creates service work order (SWO) in POS per W544; customer pays at POS — minimum 50% deposit for fabrication orders (balance on completion); POS prints SWO receipt with: order number, fabrication specifications, material list, promised completion date; system allocates raw material from inventory and creates fabrication job for Welder
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Cashier
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W988_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W988_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W988_Task8" name="Fabrication Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fabrication Execution: Welder/Fabricator retrieves raw material from yard storage per W3B; dons PPE per W140 (welding helmet, leather gloves, leather apron, safety goggles, steel-toe boots); performs fabrication: (a) cutting — measures and marks material per SWO dimensions; cuts using angle grinder with cutting disc or hacksaw for small items; (b) fitting — assembles pieces per design, clamps in position, verifies dimensions; (c) welding — MIG welds all joints with appropriate wire feed speed and voltage settings; 2-pass minimum for structural joints; (d) grinding — grinds weld beads flush where required for aesthetic finish; removes slag and spatter; (e) drilling — drills mounting holes per customer specification; (f) finish application — applies primer (zinc chromate) and/or enamel paint if included; (g) tags finished item with SWO number
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Welder/Fabricator)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 1–8 hours (varies by complexity)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W988_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W988_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W988_Task9" name="Quality Inspection &amp; Customer Handover">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Quality Inspection &amp; Customer Handover: Welder inspects: (a) dimensional accuracy — ±3mm for overall dimensions; (b) weld quality — full penetration, no porosity, no undercut, no cracks; visual inspection per AWS D1.1 (basic level); (c) finish quality — even primer/paint coverage, no rust, no grinding marks on visible surfaces; (d) structural adequacy — visual check for proper joint design and adequate weld size; failed inspection → rework or re-fabricate; customer inspects finished item and signs acceptance on SWO; customer pays remaining balance; system closes SWO and posts sale; customer loads item at yard loading zone per W438
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W988_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W988_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W988_Task10" name="Daily Station Cleanup &amp; Safety Compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Daily Station Cleanup &amp; Safety Compliance: At end of day: Welder cleans fabrication station; disconnects welding equipment; stores flammable materials (paint, thinner, welding gas) in fire-rated cabinet; cleans grinding dust and metal shavings (non-hazardous metal waste per W82); checks fire extinguisher (CO2 type, mandatory at welding station per BFP requirements per W476); inspects welding cables, ground clamp, and regulator for damage; ventilation check — welding station must have adequate natural or mechanical ventilation per DOLE standards
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Welder/Fabricator)
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 20 min/day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W988_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W988_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W988_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W988_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W988_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W988_Assoc13" sourceRef="W988_Annotation12" targetRef="W988_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W988_Flow14" sourceRef="W988_Start4" targetRef="W988_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W988_Flow15" sourceRef="W988_Task5" targetRef="W988_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W988_Flow16" sourceRef="W988_Task6" targetRef="W988_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W988_Flow17" sourceRef="W988_Task7" targetRef="W988_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W988_Flow18" sourceRef="W988_Task8" targetRef="W988_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W988_Flow19" sourceRef="W988_Task9" targetRef="W988_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W988_Flow20" sourceRef="W988_Task10" targetRef="W988_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W988_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W988_plane" bpmnElement="W_W988">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W988_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W988_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W988_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W988_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W988_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W988_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W988_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W988_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W988_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W988_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W988_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W988_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
