    <bpmn:process id="W_W1027" name="W1027. Customer AI-Powered Chatbot &amp; Virtual Shopping Assistant Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer initiates chat on buildright.com.ph, mobile app, or social media messenger (Facebook Messenger, Viber)
Frequency: ~15,000–20,000 chatbot interactions/month (one register with W1340; ~60% chatbot-resolved)
Volume: 1 session per interaction; ~40% resolve without human agent
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager
Participants: Customer, AI Chatbot (system), Human Agent (escalation), Product Content Manager, IT AI/ML Engineer
Source: workflow W1027 — Customer AI-Powered Chatbot &amp; Virtual Shopping Assistant Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1027_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1027_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1027_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1027_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1027_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1027_Lane2" name="Human Agent">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1027_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1027_Lane3" name="Product Content Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1027_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1027_Lane4" name="IT AI">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1027_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1027_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1027_Start6" name="Customer initiates chat on buildright.com.ph, mobile app, or social media messenger…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1027_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1027_Task7" name="Customer Inquiry Intake &amp; Intent Classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Inquiry Intake &amp; Intent Classification: Customer initiates chat via any channel: (a) buildright.com.ph chat widget, (b) BuildRight mobile app, (c) Facebook Messenger, (d) Viber; (e) system identifies customer (if logged in via loyalty account) with purchase history, store preference, and active orders; (f) AI chatbot processes customer message using natural language understanding (NLU): classifies intent into one of ~25 predefined categories: product_availability, price_inquiry, product_comparison, order_status, delivery_tracking, return_refund, installation_inquiry, store_location_hours, loyalty_points, payment_issue, technical_specification, project_advice, bulk_order, trade_account, complaint, promotion_inquiry, and others; (g) for multi-intent messages (&quot;Is the Bosch drill available and how does it compare to DeWalt?&quot;), system decomposes into sequential sub-intents
Responsible (R): System (AI Chatbot)
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: &lt; 5 sec (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1027_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1027_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1027_Task8" name="Automated Response &amp; Self-Service Resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automated Response &amp; Self-Service Resolution: Based on classified intent: (a) Product availability: chatbot queries real-time store inventory (customer&#x27;s nearest store from profile or asked); responds with availability, quantity on hand, and aisle location (e.g., &quot;The Bosch GSB 550 Impact Drill is available at BuildRight Davao Buhangin — 7 units in stock, Aisle 4, Power Tools section. Want me to reserve one for pickup?&quot;); (b) Price inquiry: responds with current SRP, any active promotions, trade price (if trade account), and competitor price match eligibility per W61; (c) Product comparison: generates side-by-side comparison card with specifications, price, customer ratings, and recommendation based on customer&#x27;s stated use case; (d) Order status/delivery tracking: retrieves order from system, provides current status and estimated delivery date per W592; (e) Technical specification: responds with product specs from PIM (W50) including dimensions, weight, power requirements, compatible accessories; (f) Store location/hours: responds with store address, operating hours, phone number, and Google Maps link; (g) system attempts to resolve within 3 conversational turns; if resolved, customer rates interaction (1–5 stars) and session ends
Responsible (R): System (AI Chatbot)
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 1–3 min (customer interaction)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1027_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1027_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1027_Task9" name="Human Agent Escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Human Agent Escalation: If chatbot cannot resolve within 3 turns, or customer requests human agent, or intent is flagged as high-complexity (complaint, trade account application, project pricing): (a) system transfers chat to available human agent with full conversation history and customer context; (b) customer sees &quot;Connecting you to a BuildRight team member...&quot; message; (c) target transfer time: &lt; 30 seconds during operating hours (8AM–10PM); outside hours, system offers callback or email ticket creation per W258; (d) human agent resolves per existing workflows: complaints (W41), credit application (W886), delivery issue (W1004), product question (W112); (e) upon resolution, agent tags conversation for chatbot training: &quot;resolved by human&quot; with intent category and resolution method — feeds step 5
Responsible (R): Human Agent
Accountable (A): Customer Service Supervisor
Duration: 5–15 min per escalation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1027_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1027_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1027_Task10" name="Product Content &amp; Knowledge Base Maintenance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Product Content &amp; Knowledge Base Maintenance: Product Content Manager maintains chatbot knowledge base: (a) weekly: review new product launches (W564) and update product database with specifications, comparison data, FAQs, and recommended use cases; (b) weekly: review and update promotional information, pricing changes, and store-level inventory availability logic; (c) monthly: review chatbot response accuracy metrics and identify knowledge gaps (topics where chatbot frequently escalates to human); (d) quarterly: comprehensive knowledge base audit — verify product specifications, pricing, and availability data are current; update product comparison matrices for top 500 SKUs; (e) coordinate with Category Managers for technical product training content per W920
Responsible (R): Product Content Manager
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 4–6 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1027_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1027_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1027_Task11" name="AI Model Performance Monitoring &amp; Continuous Improvement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: AI Model Performance Monitoring &amp; Continuous Improvement: IT AI/ML Engineer monitors chatbot performance: (a) daily: review escalation rate (target: &lt; 60%), customer satisfaction score (target: ≥ 4.0/5.0), and average session duration; (b) weekly: review intent classification accuracy — analyze misclassified conversations and retrain NLU model; (c) monthly: analyze &quot;unresolved&quot; conversations to identify new intent categories needed; expand response library; (d) quarterly: A/B test new response templates, product recommendation strategies, and conversation flows; (e) key metrics dashboard: resolution rate, escalation rate, average handle time (chatbot vs. human), customer satisfaction, cost per interaction (chatbot: ~PHP 5–10 vs. human agent: ~PHP 80–120)
Responsible (R): IT AI/ML Engineer
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 8–12 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1027_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1027_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1027_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1027_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1027_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: buffer-discount display rule (show &quot;available&quot; only if on-hand &gt; 3 units) and &quot;subject to availability&quot; disclaimer
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1027_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1027_Annotation13" targetRef="W1027_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1027_Flow15" sourceRef="W1027_Start6" targetRef="W1027_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1027_Flow16" sourceRef="W1027_Task7" targetRef="W1027_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1027_Flow17" sourceRef="W1027_Task8" targetRef="W1027_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1027_Flow18" sourceRef="W1027_Task9" targetRef="W1027_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1027_Flow19" sourceRef="W1027_Task10" targetRef="W1027_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1027_Flow20" sourceRef="W1027_Task11" targetRef="W1027_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1027_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1027_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1027">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1027_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1027_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
