    <bpmn:process id="W_W1045" name="W1045. Store-Level Customer PVC Pipe Cutting, Jointing &amp; Fabrication Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases PVC pipe (or brings project requirements) and requests custom-length cutting or jointing/fabrication
Frequency: ~2,000–3,000 requests/month across all stores (plumbing is 12% of SKUs, ~4,200 items; PVC pipe is the highest-volume plumbing SKU)
Volume: 1–10 cuts per customer visit; average 3–5 cuts
Owner: Plumbing Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Plumbing Section), Customer
Source: workflow W1045 — Store-Level Customer PVC Pipe Cutting, Jointing &amp; Fabrication Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1045_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1045_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1045_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1045_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1045_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1045_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1045_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1045_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1045_Start3" name="Customer purchases PVC pipe (or brings project requirements) and requests custom-length…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1045_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1045_Task4" name="Customer Requirement Intake">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Requirement Intake: Sales Associate gathers project requirements: (a) pipe material — PVC (Schedule 40, Schedule 80, DWV, conduit), CPVC (hot water), or PPR; (b) pipe diameter — ½&quot;, ¾&quot;, 1&quot;, 1¼&quot;, 1½&quot;, 2&quot;, 3&quot;, 4&quot;, 6&quot;; (c) number of pieces and lengths needed (in centimeters or inches); (d) jointing requirements — solvent-weld fittings (elbow, tee, coupling, reducer, adapter) to be pre-joined; (e) intended application — water supply, drainage, electrical conduit, irrigation, other; (f) system validates that requested lengths are achievable from standard 3m/6m stock, minimizes waste (nesting algorithm for multiple cuts)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1045_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1045_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1045_Task5" name="Cutting Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Cutting Execution: Sales Associate performs PVC cutting at dedicated cutting station in plumbing section: (a) select correct pipe from stock per diameter and schedule; (b) measure and mark cut points using tape measure and marker; (c) position pipe in cutting jig (or miter box for smaller diameters); (d) execute cut using dedicated PVC cutter (for diameters ≤2&quot;) or fine-tooth hacksaw with miter box (for diameters &gt;2&quot;); (e) deburr cut ends using chamfering tool or utility knife — remove internal and external burrs to ensure proper solvent-weld seating; (f) verify cut length within ±2mm tolerance using tape measure; (g) wipe cut ends clean of dust and shavings
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–8 min (depending on number of cuts)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1045_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1045_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1045_Task6" name="Optional Jointing / Fabrication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Optional Jointing / Fabrication: If customer requests pre-joined assemblies: (a) dry-fit all components to verify alignment before solvent cement application; (b) apply PVC primer (purple primer, mandatory for Schedule 40/80) to outside of pipe end and inside of fitting socket; (c) apply PVC solvent cement to primed surfaces; (d) insert pipe into fitting with quarter-turn twist; (e) hold joint for 15–30 seconds for initial set; (f) wipe excess cement; (g) mark joint set time: 15 min for handling, 2 hours for light pressure, 24 hours for full pressure; (h) customer takes pre-joined assembly with remaining uncut pipe lengths
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–15 min (depending on number of joints)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1045_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1045_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1045_Task7" name="Transaction Processing &amp; Waste Handling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Transaction Processing &amp; Waste Handling: (a) system charges for: full-length pipe(s) consumed (prorated by meter), fittings used, primer/cement consumed (if jointing), cutting service fee (or waived for purchases &gt;PHP 500); (b) cutting waste (offcuts &lt;30 cm) collected in store PVC recycling bin per W502 (non-hazardous waste management); (c) offcuts ≥30 cm offered to customer for potential use; (d) system updates inventory: full-length pipe decremented, cutting waste accounted per disposition code; (e) customer receives cut pieces, any pre-joined assemblies, and remaining pipe
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / POS Cashier
Accountable (A): Plumbing Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1045_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1045_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1045_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1045_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1045_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: weekly blade replacement schedule for high-volume stores; operational: PPE (gloves, safety glasses) required per W172
Owner: Plumbing Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1045_Assoc10" sourceRef="W1045_Annotation9" targetRef="W1045_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1045_Flow11" sourceRef="W1045_Start3" targetRef="W1045_Task4" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1045_Flow12" sourceRef="W1045_Task4" targetRef="W1045_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1045_Flow13" sourceRef="W1045_Task5" targetRef="W1045_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1045_Flow14" sourceRef="W1045_Task6" targetRef="W1045_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1045_Flow15" sourceRef="W1045_Task7" targetRef="W1045_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1045_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1045_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1045">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1045_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1045_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1160" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
