    <bpmn:process id="W_W1059" name="W1059. Customer Kitchen Countertop Measurement &amp; Custom Fabrication Order Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests custom kitchen countertop or bathroom vanity top measurement and fabrication
Frequency: ~1,500–2,500 orders/month across all stores (home décor &amp; furniture: 5% of SKUs; countertops are high-value items: PHP 3,000–30,000 per project)
Volume: 1 countertop per order (may include multiple sections for L-shaped or U-shaped kitchens)
Owner: Assistant Store Manager (special-order services)
Participants: Sales Associate (Home Décor Section), Special Order Coordinator, Fabrication Partner, Customer
Source: workflow W1059 — Customer Kitchen Countertop Measurement &amp; Custom Fabrication Order Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1059_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1059_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1059_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1059_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1059_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1059_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1059_Lane2" name="Special Order Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1059_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1059_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1059_Start4" name="Customer requests custom kitchen countertop or bathroom vanity top measurement and…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1059_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1059_Task5" name="Kitchen/Bathroom Layout Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Kitchen/Bathroom Layout Assessment: Sales Associate gathers project details: (a) room type — kitchen countertop, bathroom vanity top, laundry countertop, bar/counter; (b) layout shape — straight, L-shaped, U-shaped, galley, custom; (c) existing or planned cabinet dimensions — cabinet length along wall for each section; (d) counter depth — standard 600mm or custom; (e) edge profile preference — flat/eased, beveled, bullnose, half-bullnose, ogee; (f) sink type — undermount (requires sink cutout in slab), drop-in (self-rimming, no slab cutout), farmhouse/apron front (large front cutout); (g) faucet holes — number and location (1-hole, 3-hole, 4-inch spread, 8-inch spread); (h) backsplash — matching material splash (100mm or 150mm height), tile backsplash (separate per W963), or none; (i) material preference and budget
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Home Décor &amp; Furniture Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1059_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1059_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1059_Task6" name="Measurement Verification &amp; Template Requirement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Measurement Verification &amp; Template Requirement: (a) if customer provides measurements: system validates dimensions for reasonableness (typical Philippine kitchen counter lengths: 1.2m–3.6m per section; standard depth: 600mm; typical vanity: 0.6m–1.2m × 0.5m depth); (b) if customer does not have measurements: system offers two options: (i) customer takes measurements at home using provided measurement worksheet (printable from system — wall-to-wall length, depth, corner angles, sink opening dimensions, cutouts for stove/range); (ii) on-site measurement service per W442 (site technical survey &amp; measurement services) with service fee (PHP 500–1,000, waived for orders &gt;PHP 10,000); (c) for natural stone (granite, marble): system recommends on-site templating by fabricator before cutting — natural stone slabs vary in pattern and color, and site conditions may require field adjustments; (d) system creates custom specification record with all dimensions and preferences
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Special Order Coordinator
Accountable (A): Home Décor &amp; Furniture Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1059_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1059_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1059_Task7" name="Material Selection, Pricing &amp; Order Placement">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Material Selection, Pricing &amp; Order Placement: (a) system displays material options within customer&#x27;s budget: granite (PHP 3,000–8,000 per linear meter installed), quartz (PHP 5,000–15,000 per linear meter installed), laminate (PHP 1,500–4,000 per linear meter, DIY install), solid surface (PHP 6,000–20,000 per linear meter installed); (b) system calculates total cost: (i) material cost = length × per-linear-meter rate (including waste factor: 10% for straight layouts, 15–20% for L/U-shaped to account for seaming and waste at corners); (ii) fabrication cost = edge profiling (per linear meter) + sink cutout (per cutout) + faucet holes (per hole) + seaming (per joint, if multiple pieces needed); (iii) installation cost = per-linear-meter installation rate (if professional install requested per W138); (iv) delivery cost = bulky item delivery fee per W5D; (c) system generates custom order quote with 50% deposit requirement per W546; (d) customer approves quote and pays deposit at POS; (e) system transmits order to fabrication partner per W866 (vendor portal — custom order); (f) estimated lead time: laminate (3–5 days), granite/quartz fabrication (7–14 days), solid surface (10–21 days)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Home Décor &amp; Furniture Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1059_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1059_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1059_Task8" name="Fabrication, Delivery &amp; Installation Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fabrication, Delivery &amp; Installation Coordination: (a) fabrication partner manufactures countertop per specification; (b) if natural stone: fabricator performs on-site templating before cutting (arranges directly with customer); (c) upon fabrication completion, fabricator notifies BuildRight with ready date and weight/dimensions; (d) system sends delivery scheduling notification to customer; (e) customer selects delivery date; (f) for granite/quartz (heavy, fragile): system requires professional delivery per partnered logistics provider per W268 (last-mile delivery tracking); (g) if professional installation requested: system coordinates installation appointment per W138 (home installation services) — installer delivers and installs in one visit; (h) remaining 50% balance collected upon delivery/installation completion; (i) system closes custom order and logs vendor fabrication lead time for vendor scorecard per W44
Responsible (R): Special Order Coordinator / Fabrication Partner / Delivery Coordinator
Accountable (A): Home Décor &amp; Furniture Dept Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min (coordination per order)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1059_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1059_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1059_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1059_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1059_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: Assistant Store Manager (special-order services) review and approval gate
Owner: Assistant Store Manager (special-order services)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1059_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1059_Annotation10" targetRef="W1059_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1059_Flow12" sourceRef="W1059_Start4" targetRef="W1059_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1059_Flow13" sourceRef="W1059_Task5" targetRef="W1059_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1059_Flow14" sourceRef="W1059_Task6" targetRef="W1059_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1059_Flow15" sourceRef="W1059_Task7" targetRef="W1059_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1059_Flow16" sourceRef="W1059_Task8" targetRef="W1059_End9" />
    </bpmn:process>
