    <bpmn:process id="W_W1062" name="W1062. Store-Level Customer Scaffolding Rental, Safety Harness Package &amp; Delivery Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests scaffolding rental for construction, painting, or maintenance project at height
Frequency: ~800–1,200 rental requests/month across all stores (driven by Philippine construction activity and homeowner renovation projects)
Volume: 1 rental order per customer project; average 1–3 frame sets per order
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Building Materials Section), Tool Rental Coordinator, Customer
Source: workflow W1062 — Store-Level Customer Scaffolding Rental, Safety Harness Package &amp; Delivery Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1062_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1062_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1062_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1062_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1062_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1062_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1062_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1062_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1062_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1062_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1062_Start4" name="Customer requests scaffolding rental for construction, painting, or maintenance project…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1062_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1062_Task5" name="Project Height &amp; Scope Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Height &amp; Scope Assessment: Sales Associate gathers project requirements: (a) working height — highest point where worker will stand (in meters); (b) project type — interior painting, exterior painting, gutter installation, ceiling installation, wall construction, roof work, general maintenance; (c) working platform needed — number of workers on scaffold simultaneously (typical: 1–2); (d) load requirement — light duty (painting, inspection — 120 kg/m²), medium duty (general construction — 240 kg/m²); (e) site surface — concrete/flat (stable base), soil/unpaved (requires base plates and mudsills), uneven/stepped (requires adjustable jacks); (f) indoor or outdoor (indoor: aluminum mobile tower preferred; outdoor: steel frame with base jacks); (g) rental duration — days or weeks; (h) delivery needed or customer pickup (scaffold frames are bulky — steel frame set ~25 kg per frame; 3-set tower ~100 kg; requires pickup truck or delivery per W5D)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1062_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1062_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1062_Task6" name="Scaffolding Configuration &amp; Safety Package">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Scaffolding Configuration &amp; Safety Package: System recommends scaffolding configuration: (a) Number of frame tiers = working height ÷ frame height (1.7m per tier, minimum 1 tier below working platform); e.g., 4m working height = 3 tiers (1.7 + 1.7 + 1.7 = 5.1m platform height minus safety margin); (b) Frame sets: 2 frames per tier × number of tiers; (c) Cross braces: 2 per tier × number of tiers; (d) Base jacks: 2 (adjustable, for leveling); (e) Coupling pins: 2 per tier connection; (f) Walk planks: 1–2 per platform level (steel or wood, rated for load); (g) Guardrails: top rail (1.0m above platform) + mid-rail (0.5m above platform) per DOLE DO 13 safety standard; (h) Toe boards: 150mm minimum height at platform edge per DOLE DO 13; (i) Safety harness package (mandatory for work &gt;3m per DOLE): full-body harness + shock-absorbing lanyard + anchor point; (j) Hard hat: mandatory per DOLE DO 13 for all construction work; (k) system checks rental inventory availability per store per W533
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1062_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1062_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1062_Task7" name="Rental Agreement, Deposit &amp; Safety Waiver">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Rental Agreement, Deposit &amp; Safety Waiver: (a) system generates rental agreement with: rental item list (each frame, brace, jack, plank — serialized with asset tags), daily/weekly rental rate per item, rental duration, total rental cost, replacement cost per item (for damage/loss), deposit amount (typically 50% of replacement cost or PHP 5,000–20,000 depending on configuration); (b) customer signs safety acknowledgment per DOLE DO 13: (i) scaffold must be erected per manufacturer instructions and DOLE standards; (ii) maximum load rating must not be exceeded; (iii) safety harness must be worn and properly anchored at all times when working &gt;3m; (iv) scaffold must be inspected before each use; (v) BuildRight Depot is not liable for injury resulting from improper scaffold erection, overloading, or failure to use safety equipment; (c) system collects deposit at POS per W546 (deposit &amp; progress payment collection) — held as customer deposit per W94; (d) system records rental agreement with customer ID, rental start date, expected return date
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / POS Cashier
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1062_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1062_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1062_Task8" name="Delivery (If Requested) &amp; Customer Handoff">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Delivery (If Requested) &amp; Customer Handoff: (a) if delivery requested: system schedules delivery per W5D (home delivery scheduling) with bulky item delivery fee; (b) delivery team loads scaffold components and safety equipment; (c) upon delivery, customer or customer&#x27;s representative signs delivery receipt acknowledging receipt of all items per serialized list; (d) if customer pickup: Sales Associate stages rental items at store loading area per W950 (vehicle loading assistance); (e) customer receives: rental agreement copy, safety instruction sheet, scaffold assembly diagram (manufacturer&#x27;s instructions), and emergency contact number
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Delivery Coordinator
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1062_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1062_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1062_Task9" name="Return, Inspection &amp; Deposit Refund">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Return, Inspection &amp; Deposit Refund: (a) customer returns scaffold components on or before rental end date; (b) Sales Associate inspects each serialized component: (i) frames: no bends, cracks, or weld damage; (ii) cross braces: no bends, locking pins functional; (iii) base jacks: threads functional, no corrosion; (iv) walk planks: no cracks, rot, or excessive wear; (v) safety harness: no cuts, fraying, or chemical damage; webbing intact; (vi) hard hat: no cracks, dents, or UV degradation; (c) system logs return condition per asset tag; (d) if all items returned in good condition: system releases full deposit refund per W101 (customer refund &amp; credit processing); (e) if items damaged or missing: system deducts replacement cost from deposit per rental agreement terms; (f) system calculates final rental charge: (actual rental days × daily rate) or (rental weeks × weekly rate, whichever is lower); (g) system settles: deposit minus (rental charge + any damage deductions); (h) system updates rental asset inventory per W399 and rental equipment maintenance schedule per W650 (warehouse equipment preventive maintenance adapted for rental assets)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Tool Rental Coordinator
Accountable (A): Lumber &amp; Building Materials Dept Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1062_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1062_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1062_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1062_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1062_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Lumber &amp; Building Materials Department Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
