    <bpmn:process id="W_W1086" name="W1086. Customer Construction Waste Disposal &amp; Skip/Dumpster Rental Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: B2B contractor or B2C renovation customer requests construction waste disposal solution, or BuildRight proactively offers waste disposal coordination as a value-added service during large project quotation (W162)
Frequency: ~1,500–2,500 coordination requests/month across all stores (construction waste disposal is a high-need service for BuildRight&#x27;s B2B contractor base of ~5,200 trade accounts)
Volume: 1 skip/dumpster rental coordination per project
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Trade Counter), Partner Waste Hauler, Customer
Source: workflow W1086 — Customer Construction Waste Disposal &amp; Skip/Dumpster Rental Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1086_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1086_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1086_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1086_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1086_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1086_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1086_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1086_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1086_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1086_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1086_Start4" name="B2B contractor or B2C renovation customer requests construction waste disposal solution…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1086_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1086_Task5" name="Waste Volume Estimation &amp; Skip Size Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Waste Volume Estimation &amp; Skip Size Recommendation: Sales Associate estimates waste volume based on the customer&#x27;s project: (a) project type: bathroom renovation (2–4 cubic meters of waste), kitchen renovation (3–6 cu.m.), full house renovation (10–30 cu.m.), new construction site clearance (20–50+ cu.m.), roofing replacement (5–10 cu.m.); (b) waste types expected: concrete/hollow block rubble, tiles/ceramics, lumber/plywood scraps, metal (rebar, GI sheets), plastic (PVC, packaging), paint/chemical containers; (c) system recommends skip/dumpster size: small skip (2 cu.m. — bathroom reno), medium skip (5 cu.m. — kitchen/single room reno), large skip (10 cu.m. — major renovation), or roll-off container (15–20 cu.m. — construction site); (d) system queries partner hauler availability in the customer&#x27;s area for the requested dates
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1086_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1086_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1086_Task6" name="Partner Hauler Booking &amp; Pricing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Partner Hauler Booking &amp; Pricing: System coordinates with vetted partner waste haulers: (a) system displays available haulers in the customer&#x27;s delivery area with: hauler name, LGU-registered permit number, available skip sizes, rental period (standard: 7 days), pricing (delivery, rental, pickup, disposal fee), and customer rating; (b) system auto-selects best-value hauler based on price, availability, and rating; (c) for B2B trade accounts: system applies pre-negotiated corporate rates; (d) waste classification: system flags if waste includes regulated materials (paint/chemical containers per W236 hazmat, asbestos-containing materials requiring special handling); (e) booking confirmed: hauler name, skip size, delivery date, delivery address, rental period, pickup date, total price; (f) system sends booking confirmation to customer (SMS/email) and to partner hauler via API integration
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1086_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1086_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1086_Task7" name="Documentation &amp; Compliance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Documentation &amp; Compliance: System generates required documentation: (a) waste disposal manifest: description of waste types, estimated volume, origin address, destination disposal site (LGU-approved), hauler permit number; (b) DENR compliance: for projects exceeding 5 cu.m. of construction waste, system notes that the hauler must deliver to a DENR-registered disposal facility per RA 9003; (c) LGU permit reminder: some LGUs require a temporary waste disposal permit for construction projects; system reminds customer to check with their barangay; (d) hazardous material handling: if paint cans, solvents, or chemicals are in the waste stream, system generates separate hazmat handling instructions per W236 and recommends a specialized hazmat hauler; (e) all documentation attached to customer&#x27;s project order in ERP for traceability
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1086_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1086_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1086_Task8" name="Delivery, Monitoring &amp; Pickup Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Delivery, Monitoring &amp; Pickup Coordination: (a) system sends automated delivery reminder to customer and hauler 1 day before scheduled skip delivery; (b) on delivery day: hauler delivers skip to customer&#x27;s site, customer signs delivery receipt; system logs delivery confirmation via hauler API or manual update; (c) during rental period: system monitors rental days remaining; sends reminder to customer and hauler 1 day before scheduled pickup; (d) customer may request extension via BuildRight app or store — system checks hauler availability and adjusts pricing for extended rental; (e) on pickup day: hauler collects skip, transports waste to LGU-approved disposal facility, obtains disposal facility receipt (proof of legal disposal); (f) hauler uploads disposal receipt to BuildRight system; (g) system triggers customer satisfaction survey
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: Ongoing monitoring (automated) + 5 min per extension request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1086_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1086_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1086_Task9" name="Settlement, Hauler Payment &amp; Revenue Recognition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Settlement, Hauler Payment &amp; Revenue Recognition: (a) system invoices customer: skip rental total (delivery + rental + pickup + disposal fee) + BuildRight coordination fee (5–8% of hauler charge); (b) for trade account customers: added to monthly billing statement per W8; (c) for walk-in/B2C customers: payment at POS or via payment link; (d) system triggers payment to partner hauler: hauler receives total amount minus BuildRight coordination fee; payment per agreed terms (Net 15 or Net 30); (e) revenue recognition: BuildRight records coordination fee as service revenue; (f) monthly: system generates partner hauler performance report: on-time delivery rate, on-time pickup rate, customer satisfaction score, compliance incidents (missing disposal receipts); (g) quarterly: Trade Counter Supervisor reviews hauler performance and recommends continuation or replacement of underperforming haulers
Responsible (R): System / Trade Counter Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Per-transaction settlement: automated; Monthly review: 1–2 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1086_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1086_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1086_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1086_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1086_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: per W236; operational: must maintain an LGU-specific compliance rules database
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1086_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1086_Annotation11" targetRef="W1086_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1086_Flow13" sourceRef="W1086_Start4" targetRef="W1086_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1086_Flow14" sourceRef="W1086_Task5" targetRef="W1086_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1086_Flow15" sourceRef="W1086_Task6" targetRef="W1086_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1086_Flow16" sourceRef="W1086_Task7" targetRef="W1086_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1086_Flow17" sourceRef="W1086_Task8" targetRef="W1086_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1086_Flow18" sourceRef="W1086_Task9" targetRef="W1086_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1086_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1086_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1086">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1086_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1086_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1086_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1086_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
