    <bpmn:process id="W_W1088" name="W1088. Customer Mortgage &amp; Housing Loan Partner Bank Referral Desk Operations" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer inquiring about major home construction, renovation, or appliance purchase expresses interest in financing options, or Sales Associate identifies that the customer&#x27;s project budget exceeds their immediate purchasing capacity
Frequency: ~3,000–5,000 referral interactions/month across all stores (driven by B2C customers undertaking major home improvement projects with average project cost of PHP 50,000–500,000)
Volume: 1 referral per customer interaction
Owner: Customer Service Representative
Participants: Sales Associate, Customer Service Representative, Partner Bank/Financing Representative
Source: workflow W1088 — Customer Mortgage &amp; Housing Loan Partner Bank Referral Desk Operations</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1088_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1088_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1088_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1088_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1088_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1088_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1088_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1088_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1088_Lane3" name="Customer Service Rep">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1088_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1088_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1088_Start5" name="Customer inquiring about major home construction, renovation, or appliance purchase…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1088_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1088_Task6" name="Customer Financing Need Identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Customer Financing Need Identification: (a) Sales Associate identifies financing need during project consultation: customer mentions budget constraint, asks about installment options, or the project estimate exceeds PHP 50,000; (b) Associate introduces financing options: &quot;BuildRight has partner banks that offer home improvement loans with competitive rates. Would you like me to connect you with our financing desk?&quot;; (c) Customer Service Representative (or dedicated Financing Desk Associate in high-volume stores) conducts preliminary assessment: (i) customer type: employed, self-employed, OFW, pensioner; (ii) estimated project cost; (iii) desired loan amount; (iv) preferred repayment term; (v) existing bank relationships; (vi) Pag-IBIG membership status; (d) system displays recommended financing options based on assessment
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Customer Service Representative
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1088_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1088_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1088_Task7" name="Financing Option Matching &amp; Partner Bank Selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Financing Option Matching &amp; Partner Bank Selection: System matches customer profile to available financing products: (a) Bank Home Improvement Loan — for project costs PHP 100K+: requirements include proof of income (latest ITR or BIR Form 2316, latest 3 months payslips, COE), 2 valid government IDs, proof of billing address, marriage certificate (if applicable); processing time: 5–7 banking days; banks: BDO Home Loan, BPI Family Savings, Metrobank Home Improvement; (b) Pag-IBIG Home Improvement Loan — for qualified Pag-IBIG members: requires 24 monthly contributions, updated membership, property titled under borrower&#x27;s name or relative&#x27;s name with consent; processing time: 10–15 working days; (c) Credit Card Installment — for purchases PHP 5,000+: instant approval, 0% interest for 3/6/12 months (during promotional periods), no additional documents; (d) In-Store Financing (Partner Bank Desk) — some stores host a partner bank representative 2–3 days per week for on-the-spot application processing; (e) system displays comparison table: product, amount range, interest rate, term, processing time, monthly payment estimate
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Customer Service Representative
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1088_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1088_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1088_Task8" name="Application Facilitation &amp; Document Assistance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Application Facilitation &amp; Document Assistance: (a) Customer Service Representative assists customer with financing application: (i) provides partner bank application form (pre-printed with BuildRight referral code for commission tracking); (ii) reviews customer&#x27;s documents for completeness; (iii) for Pag-IBIG loans: assists with HDMF form verification and member contribution printout; (iv) for bank loans: explains income documentation requirements and assists with self-employed customer&#x27;s financial statement preparation (basic guidance); (b) for in-store bank desk days: schedules appointment with partner bank representative at the store; (c) system generates project cost estimate on BuildRight letterhead (required by banks as proof of purpose) linked to quotation per W162; (d) Customer Service Representative submits application to partner bank via email or in-person (on bank desk days); (e) system logs referral in CRM with: customer name, project description, estimated loan amount, partner bank, submission date, referral code
Responsible (R): Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Customer Service Representative
Duration: 15–25 min per application</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1088_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1088_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1088_Task9" name="Loan Tracking &amp; Purchase Conversion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Loan Tracking &amp; Purchase Conversion: (a) system tracks loan application status via partner bank API (where available) or manual status update by Customer Service Representative; (b) system sends periodic status updates to customer: &quot;Your home improvement loan application with [Bank] is being processed. Expected decision by [date].&quot;; (c) upon loan approval: system notifies Customer Service Representative and Sales Associate who initiated the referral; (d) Customer Service Representative contacts customer: &quot;Congratulations! Your loan has been approved for PHP [amount]. You can now proceed with your project purchase at BuildRight.&quot;; (e) customer returns to store (or purchases online) to complete the material order; system links the original project estimate to the final purchase; (f) bank disburses loan amount: either directly to customer&#x27;s account (customer pays BuildRight) or via manager&#x27;s check payable to BuildRight (for large B2B projects); (g) BuildRight earns referral commission from partner bank (typically 0.5–1.5% of loan amount, paid quarterly by the bank)
Responsible (R): System / Customer Service Rep
Accountable (A): Customer Service Representative
Duration: Ongoing: ~10 min per status check/approval follow-up</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1088_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1088_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1088_Task10" name="Monthly Referral Performance Reporting &amp; Partner Bank Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly Referral Performance Reporting &amp; Partner Bank Review: (a) system generates monthly referral performance report: number of referrals by store, number of applications submitted, approval rate, total loan amount originated, average project purchase value (financed vs. non-financed), referral commission earned; (b) Store Manager reviews financing desk performance; (c) quarterly: Category Manager (Appliances/Services) reviews partner bank relationships: approval rates, commission payments, customer satisfaction, competitive rate benchmarking; (d) annual: VP Merchandising negotiates referral commission rates and exclusive promotional terms with partner banks (e.g., 0% installment promos during BuildRight sale events per W13)
Responsible (R): System / Store Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Monthly report: 30 min; Quarterly review: 2–3 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1088_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1088_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1088_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1088_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1088_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: Customer Service Representative review and approval gate
Owner: Customer Service Representative</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1088_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1088_Annotation12" targetRef="W1088_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
