    <bpmn:process id="W_W1094" name="W1094. Customer Construction Equipment Rental Partner Coordination &amp; Booking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests construction equipment rental (excavator, backhoe, concrete mixer, scaffolding, generator, welding machine, jackhammer, plate compactor, etc.) during a project material purchase, or accesses the equipment rental section via the BuildRight app or store kiosk
Frequency: ~1,500–2,500 booking requests/month across all stores (equipment rental is a growing value-added service for BuildRight&#x27;s B2B contractor base)
Volume: 1 equipment rental booking per request
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Trade Counter), Equipment Rental Partner, Customer
Source: workflow W1094 — Customer Construction Equipment Rental Partner Coordination &amp; Booking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1094_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1094_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1094_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1094_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1094_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1094_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1094_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1094_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1094_Lane3" name="Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1094_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1094_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1094_Start5" name="Customer requests construction equipment rental (excavator, backhoe, concrete mixer…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1094_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1094_Task6" name="Equipment Requirement Identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Equipment Requirement Identification: Sales Associate identifies equipment needs based on the customer&#x27;s project: (a) project type: foundation excavation (mini-excavator + dump truck for soil hauling), concrete pouring (portable mixer + vibrator + trowel), multi-story construction (scaffolding + material hoist), demolition (jackhammer + concrete saw), roofing (scaffolding + generator for power tools); (b) equipment specifications: capacity/size (excavator: 1-ton mini for tight spaces, 3-ton for open sites), power source (electric — requires on-site power, or diesel/petrol — self-contained), duration needed (daily, weekly, monthly rates); (c) site conditions: accessibility (narrow alley in urban barangay limits equipment width to &lt;1.0m), ground conditions (soft soil may require tracked vs. wheeled equipment), and noise restrictions (residential area may limit operating hours per LGU ordinance); (d) operator requirement: does the customer need an equipment operator (required for excavators and heavy equipment) or will they self-operate (for mixers, generators, jackhammers)?
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1094_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1094_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1094_Task7" name="Partner Matching &amp; Availability Check">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Partner Matching &amp; Availability Check: (a) system queries equipment rental partners in the customer&#x27;s service area per W600 (service contractor accreditation — extended to equipment rental companies); (b) system displays available equipment: equipment type, capacity, brand/model, rental rate (daily/weekly/monthly), operator availability (with or without), delivery/pickup availability, partner name and rating; (c) for equipment requiring certified operators (excavators, backhoes, forklifts): system verifies partner provides TESDA-certified operators per Philippine DOLE regulations; (d) system auto-selects best-value option (lowest total cost = rental rate + delivery + operator if needed, weighted by partner rating and availability); (e) for high-demand equipment during peak construction season (January–May dry season): system may show limited availability and offer waitlist or alternative equipment options
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1094_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1094_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1094_Task8" name="Booking Confirmation &amp; Contract Generation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Booking Confirmation &amp; Contract Generation: (a) system generates equipment rental booking: equipment type, model, rental period (start date/time, end date/time), rental rate, operator (if applicable), delivery address, site contact person, total estimated cost (rental + delivery + operator + fuel surcharge if applicable); (b) system generates rental agreement with terms: (i) damage liability (customer responsible for damage beyond normal wear); (ii) late return charges (1.5× daily rate per day late); (iii) fuel policy (diesel/petrol equipment returned with same fuel level); (iv) insurance requirement (customer must provide evidence of project insurance or purchase rental insurance from partner); (v) operator conduct (for partner-supplied operators: customer may not direct operator to perform unsafe operations); (vi) cancellation policy (free cancellation 24+ hours before delivery; 50% charge for same-day cancellation); (c) customer signs rental agreement (digital or wet signature); (d) system sends confirmation to customer and partner; (e) for trade account customers: rental charges billed to account per W8; for B2C customers: pre-authorization hold on credit card or cash deposit at POS
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 5–8 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1094_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1094_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1094_Task9" name="Delivery, Monitoring &amp; Return Coordination">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Delivery, Monitoring &amp; Return Coordination: (a) partner delivers equipment to customer site on scheduled date; (b) customer and partner conduct joint equipment inspection at delivery: document existing damage (photos + written record), verify fuel level, test operation; (c) system logs delivery confirmation; (d) during rental period: system monitors rental duration and sends return reminders 24 hours before scheduled return; (e) for rental extensions: customer notifies BuildRight (via app, phone, or store) — system checks partner availability for extension and adjusts billing; (f) at return: customer and partner conduct joint return inspection: verify equipment condition matches delivery inspection, fuel level, and hours meter reading; (g) system logs return confirmation and final charges; (h) any damage disputes: documented with photos, assessed by partner, and charged to customer per rental agreement terms
Responsible (R): Partner / System
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: Delivery/return inspection: 15–30 min each; Monitoring: automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1094_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1094_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1094_Task10" name="Settlement &amp; Partner Performance Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Settlement &amp; Partner Performance Management: (a) system generates final rental invoice: rental charges (actual duration × rate), delivery/pickup charges, operator charges, fuel charges, damage charges (if any), taxes, total; (b) for trade accounts: added to monthly billing; for B2C: credit card pre-auth converted to actual charge or deposit refunded less charges; (c) BuildRight earns coordination fee: 5–10% of total rental charge; (d) system updates partner performance record: on-time delivery rate, equipment condition rating, customer satisfaction score, damage dispute rate; (e) quarterly: Trade Counter Supervisor reviews partner performance; poorly rated partners are placed on probation or replaced
Responsible (R): System / Trade Counter Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Per-booking settlement: automated; Quarterly review: 2–3 hrs</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1094_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1094_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1094_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1094_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1094_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: must manage customer expectations and offer alternatives
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1094_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1094_Annotation12" targetRef="W1094_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1094_Flow14" sourceRef="W1094_Start5" targetRef="W1094_Task6" />
