    <bpmn:process id="W_W1101" name="W1101. Store-Level Customer Door &amp; Window Security Grille Custom Fabrication Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests custom-made security grilles for doors or windows during a building material purchase, or Sales Associate identifies the need during a fencing/security consultation per W1084
Frequency: ~3,000–5,000 coordination requests/month across all stores (security grilles are a standard feature in Philippine homes — nearly every ground-floor window and door has steel security grilles)
Volume: 1 fabrication project per coordination (typically covering 4–15 windows + 1–2 doors)
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor
Participants: Sales Associate (Trade Counter / Lumber &amp; Building Materials), Fabrication Service Partner (accredited welder/fabricator), Customer
Source: workflow W1101 — Store-Level Customer Door &amp; Window Security Grille Custom Fabrication Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1101_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1101_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1101_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1101_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1101_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1101_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1101_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1101_Lane3" name="Trade Counter Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1101_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1101_Lane4" name="Fabrication Partner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1101_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1101_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1101_Start6" name="Customer requests custom-made security grilles for doors or windows during a building…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1101_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1101_Task7" name="Measurement Requirements &amp; Design Specifications">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Measurement Requirements &amp; Design Specifications: (a) Sales Associate gathers grille specifications: (i) number of windows requiring grilles and approximate dimensions (width × height per window); (ii) number of doors requiring security doors and approximate dimensions; (iii) bar style preference: vertical bars only (most common and cost-effective), vertical + horizontal (cross-hatch for higher security), or decorative scrollwork (premium); (iv) bar spacing: standard (100–120mm between bars — prevents head entry) or tight (80mm — maximum security for high-risk areas); (v) frame material: flat bar (¼&quot; × 1&quot;) or angle bar (1&quot; × 1&quot; × ¼&quot;); (vi) bar material: square tube (16mm, 20mm) — modern look, or round bar (12mm, 16mm) — traditional; (vii) finish: primer + black enamel (standard), primer + color-matched enamel (per W1093), powder coating (premium), or stainless steel (highest grade, coastal areas); (viii) hinged or fixed: hinged grilles for windows that need opening (for cleaning or emergency egress) vs. fixed grilles; (ix) locking mechanism for hinged grilles: barrel bolt, padlock hasp, or keyed lock
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 8–12 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1101_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1101_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1101_Task8" name="Fabrication Partner Matching &amp; Quotation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Fabrication Partner Matching &amp; Quotation: (a) system queries accredited fabrication partners (welding shops) in the customer&#x27;s area per W600 (service contractor accreditation); (b) system generates material cost estimate: (i) steel material: flat bar × total perimeter length (all windows/doors) + square tube/round bar × total bar count × standard bar length; (ii) welding consumables: welding rods/electrodes (E6013 or E7018), cutting gas (if oxy-acetylene); (iii) paint: anti-rust primer (red oxide, 1 coat) + enamel paint (2 coats) — quantity per surface area of finished grilles; (iv) hardware: expansion bolts (4 per window grille, 6 per door grille), hinges (2 per hinged grille), barrel bolts/locks, and miscellaneous (wire brush, sandpaper for surface prep); (c) system estimates fabrication labor: cutting, welding, grinding, and finishing — based on linear meters of welding and number of pieces; (d) system estimates installation labor: delivery, fitting, anchoring, and cleanup; (e) total project cost estimate = material cost + fabrication labor + installation labor; (f) typical cost ranges: window grille (1.0m × 1.2m, standard vertical bars, primer + black enamel): PHP 2,500–4,000 per window; door security gate (0.9m × 2.1m, hinged with lock): PHP 6,000–12,000 per door
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1101_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1101_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1101_Task9" name="On-Site Measurement &amp; Fabrication Order">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: On-Site Measurement &amp; Fabrication Order: (a) for accuracy: Associate recommends that the fabrication partner perform on-site measurement before fabrication (Philippine window openings often deviate from planned dimensions by 10–30mm); (b) system schedules on-site measurement visit: partner visits customer&#x27;s home within 2–3 days to measure every opening precisely; (c) partner sends measurement sheet to BuildRight system: exact width, height, and any irregularities (arched top, angled sill, pipe/conduit obstruction); (d) system generates final fabrication order with precise dimensions and updates material quantities accordingly; (e) material delivery: BuildRight delivers steel, paint, and hardware to the fabrication partner&#x27;s workshop (not to the customer&#x27;s home — the partner fabricates at their workshop) per W668
Responsible (R): Trade Counter Supervisor / Fabrication Partner
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: Measurement visit: 1–2 hrs; Order update: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1101_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1101_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1101_Task10" name="Fabrication, Quality Check &amp; Installation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Fabrication, Quality Check &amp; Installation: (a) fabrication partner fabricates grilles per the measurement sheet: (i) cuts flat bar and square tube/round bar to size; (ii) assembles frame by welding; (iii) welds vertical bars at specified spacing; (iv) grinds all welds smooth (no sharp edges); (v) installs hinges and lock hardware (for hinged grilles); (vi) applies anti-rust primer (1 coat) and enamel paint (2 coats) with drying time between coats; (b) fabrication timeline: 3–7 days depending on scope (4–6 windows: 3 days; 10–15 windows + 2 doors: 5–7 days); (c) Trade Counter Supervisor performs quality check (or partner self-certifies per W600 accreditation): (i) dimensions match measurement sheet (±5mm tolerance); (ii) weld quality: no visible gaps, porosity, or undercut; (iii) bar spacing uniform and within specification; (iv) paint coverage: complete, no bare steel visible, smooth finish; (v) hinges operate smoothly, locks engage properly; (d) partner delivers and installs grilles at customer&#x27;s home: anchors to wall with expansion bolts, seals around frame with silicone sealant, and verifies operation
Responsible (R): Fabrication Partner / Trade Counter Supervisor
Accountable (A): Trade Counter Supervisor
Duration: Fabrication: 3–7 days; Installation: 1 day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1101_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1101_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1101_Task11" name="Customer Acceptance, Settlement &amp; Warranty">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Customer Acceptance, Settlement &amp; Warranty: (a) customer inspects installed grilles: verifies fit, finish, operation, and security; (b) customer signs acceptance; (c) system generates final invoice: material cost (BuildRight) + fabrication labor (partner) + installation labor (partner) = total project cost; (d) payment: (i) for trade account customers: added to monthly billing per W8; (ii) for B2C customers: 50% deposit at order placement, 50% upon installation acceptance; (e) BuildRight pays partner: fabrication + installation labor minus BuildRight coordination fee (8–12%); (f) warranty: fabrication partner provides 1-year workmanship warranty (weld integrity, paint adhesion); BuildRight provides material quality warranty per manufacturer terms; (g) system sends customer satisfaction survey and updates partner performance record per W600
Responsible (R): System / Trade Counter Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: Settlement: automated; Satisfaction: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1101_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1101_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1101_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1101_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1101_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Trade Counter / Pro Desk Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1101_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1101_Annotation13" targetRef="W1101_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
