    <bpmn:process id="W_W1113" name="W1113. Customer E-Gift Card Purchase &amp; Digital Delivery" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases an e-gift card via BuildRight website, mobile app, or in-store
Frequency: ~3,000–6,000 e-gift card purchases/month (within the W1476 program register; growing segment, especially during holidays)
Volume: 1–5 e-gift cards per purchase transaction
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager
Participants: Customer (purchaser), Customer (recipient), Ecommerce Platform, POS System, Finance (GL)
Source: workflow W1113 — Customer E-Gift Card Purchase &amp; Digital Delivery</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1113_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1113_Lane1" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1113_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1113_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1113_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1113_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1113_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1113_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1113_Lane3" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1113_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1113_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1113_Start5" name="Customer purchases an e-gift card via BuildRight website, mobile app, or in-store">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1113_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1113_Task6" name="E-Gift Card Purchase &amp; Personalization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: E-Gift Card Purchase &amp; Personalization: (a) customer selects e-gift card on BuildRight website/app or at POS: (i) chooses denomination: PHP 500, PHP 1,000, PHP 2,000, PHP 5,000, or custom amount (min PHP 200, max PHP 50,000); (ii) selects design/theme: Birthday, Wedding, Housewarming, Congratulations, Holiday, Generic; (iii) enters recipient name, email address, and mobile number; (iv) writes personal message (max 200 characters); (v) selects delivery date: immediate or scheduled future date (up to 90 days ahead); (vi) pays via CC, GCash, Maya, or bank transfer; (b) system validates: purchaser&#x27;s payment is successful, recipient email/mobile is valid format, total purchase amount is within anti-money laundering limits (single purchase ≤ PHP 50,000 per BSP guidelines)
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1113_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1113_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1113_Task7" name="E-Gift Card Generation &amp; Digital Delivery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: E-Gift Card Generation &amp; Digital Delivery: (a) system generates unique e-gift card: 16-digit card number, 4-digit PIN, QR code, and barcode — all cryptographically generated with checksum validation; (b) system creates personalized e-gift card image with selected design, recipient name, personal message, sender name, and amount; (c) system records liability: debit Cash/Receivable, credit Gift Card Liability (deferred revenue) at full face value; (d) delivery: (i) email with e-gift card image as attachment and embedded redemption instructions; (ii) SMS to recipient&#x27;s mobile with shortened link to e-gift card; (iii) both include: card number, PIN, QR code, expiration date (24 months from purchase per BuildRight policy), terms and conditions, and customer service contact; (e) purchaser receives confirmation email with delivery status; (f) for scheduled delivery, system queues the email/SMS for the selected date
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): automated
Duration: &lt; 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1113_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1113_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1113_Task8" name="E-Gift Card Redemption at POS or Online">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: E-Gift Card Redemption at POS or Online: (a) recipient uses e-gift card at any BuildRight store or online: (i) In-Store: customer presents e-gift card QR code on mobile screen at POS; cashier scans QR code; system validates: card number exists, PIN matches, card has remaining balance, card is not expired; balance displayed on cashier screen; customer enters PIN on pin pad for security; transaction amount deducted from card balance; (ii) Online: customer enters card number and PIN at checkout; system validates and applies available balance; remaining balance (if any) displayed after transaction; (b) system updates: (i) gift card liability reduced by transaction amount; (ii) revenue recognized at redemption (not at purchase, per revenue recognition per W487 PFRS 15); (iii) remaining balance tracked on card record; (c) partial redemption is allowed; remaining balance stays on the card for future use; (d) if transaction amount exceeds gift card balance, customer pays the difference via another tender type (split payment per multi-tender POS support)
Responsible (R): Cashier / System / Customer
Accountable (A): Store Manager / Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 2–3 min additional at POS</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1113_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1113_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1113_Task9" name="E-Gift Card Balance Inquiry &amp; Re-Send">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: E-Gift Card Balance Inquiry &amp; Re-Send: (a) customer can check balance online (buildright.com.ph/giftcard-balance), via mobile app, or at any store POS; (b) if recipient did not receive the e-gift card email/SMS: purchaser can request re-send from order confirmation page or by contacting customer service (W258); system re-sends to the same or updated email/mobile; (c) e-gift card cannot be re-sent to a different recipient after original delivery (to prevent fraud)
Responsible (R): System / Customer Service
Accountable (A): automated
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1113_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1113_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1113_Task10" name="Monthly E-Gift Card Reconciliation &amp; Liability Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly E-Gift Card Reconciliation &amp; Liability Reporting: (a) Finance performs monthly reconciliation: (i) total e-gift card liability (unredeemed balance); (ii) redemption rate by cohort (month of purchase vs. month of redemption); (iii) breakage estimate (expected unredeemed portion recognized as revenue per historical patterns); (iv) fraud incidents and chargebacks; (b) system auto-recognizes breakage revenue for cards older than 24 months (expired, unredeemed) per W939 (store credit expiration management); (c) report submitted to CFO for liability management and program health assessment
Responsible (R): System / Finance
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1113_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1113_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1113_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1113_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1113_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1113_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1113_Annotation12" targetRef="W1113_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1113_Flow14" sourceRef="W1113_Start5" targetRef="W1113_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1113_Flow15" sourceRef="W1113_Task6" targetRef="W1113_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1113_Flow16" sourceRef="W1113_Task7" targetRef="W1113_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1113_Flow17" sourceRef="W1113_Task8" targetRef="W1113_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1113_Flow18" sourceRef="W1113_Task9" targetRef="W1113_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1113_Flow19" sourceRef="W1113_Task10" targetRef="W1113_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1113_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1113_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1113">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1113_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1113_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
