    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1114" name="W1114. Customer Product Availability Real-Time Stock Lookup &amp; Reservation Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer inquiry about product availability via mobile app, website, phone call, or in-store associate
Frequency: ~50,000–80,000 stock lookup requests/month across all channels
Volume: 1–5 SKUs per lookup
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager (digital channels); Customer Service Representative (phone/in-store)
Participants: Customer, Sales Associate, Customer Service Representative, E-commerce Platform
Source: workflow W1114 — Customer Product Availability Real-Time Stock Lookup &amp; Reservation Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1114_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1114_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1114_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1114_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1114_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1114_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1114_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1114_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1114_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1114_Start4" name="Customer inquiry about product availability via mobile app, website, phone call, or…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1114_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1114_Task5" name="Real-Time Stock Inquiry">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Real-Time Stock Inquiry: (a) customer initiates stock lookup via: (i) BuildRight mobile app — search by SKU, barcode scan, or product name; app shows availability at all stores within selected radius (default: 20km); (ii) website — product page shows &quot;Check availability at your store&quot; with store selector dropdown; (iii) phone call to customer service (W259) — agent looks up SKU in system; (iv) in-store — Sales Associate checks via handheld RF device or store tablet; (b) system queries real-time inventory: for each store within range, displays: (i) current available-to-promise (ATP) quantity (on-hand minus reserved for existing orders); (ii) stock status indicator: ● In Stock (≥ display threshold), ○ Low Stock (1–3 units), ◌ Out of Stock; (iii) aisle/section location within the store (e.g., &quot;Aisle 3, Bay 7 — Plumbing&quot;); (iv) next expected replenishment date (from the ASCP planning run — fit-gap C5); (c) for high-demand items with limited stock, system shows &quot;X other customers are viewing this item at [Store]&quot; to create urgency
Responsible (R): System / Customer
Accountable (A): automated
Duration: &lt; 3 seconds</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1114_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1114_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1114_Task6" name="Reservation Request &amp; Stock Hold">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Reservation Request &amp; Stock Hold: (a) if item is in stock, customer can choose to reserve: (i) select quantity and store; (ii) choose reservation duration: 2 hours (free), 4 hours (free), end of today (free), or until store closing tomorrow (PHP 50 reservation fee, refundable upon purchase); (iii) provide name and mobile number for notification; (b) system creates a stock reservation: (i) ATP quantity reduced by reserved amount (visible to other customers as &quot;X reserved&quot;); (ii) customer receives SMS confirmation with reservation ID, item, quantity, store name, and hold expiration time; (iii) store receiving desk and customer service counter receive reservation notification; (c) reservation limits per customer: max 5 reservations active at any time, max 10 units per SKU per reservation, max reservation value of PHP 100,000
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1114_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1114_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1114_Task7" name="Reservation Fulfillment &amp; Expiry Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Reservation Fulfillment &amp; Expiry Management: (a) customer arrives at store and presents reservation ID (SMS on phone) at customer service counter; (b) CSR verifies reservation: (i) reservation ID matches active reservation; (ii) customer name/ID matches; (iii) reservation has not expired; (c) CSR directs customer to the item&#x27;s aisle location or retrieves from backroom if pre-staged; (d) customer proceeds to POS for purchase — reservation ID scanned, hold released, inventory deducted; (e) if customer does not arrive before expiration: (i) system automatically releases the reservation; (ii) ATP quantity restored; (iii) customer receives SMS notification: &quot;Your reservation for [Item] at [Store] has expired. The item is now available to other customers.&quot;; (iv) if reservation fee was paid (PHP 50): fee forfeited and recorded as miscellaneous revenue
Responsible (R): System / Customer Service Representative
Accountable (A): Customer Service Representative
Duration: 3–5 min at pickup</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1114_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1114_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1114_Task8" name="Stock Lookup Analytics &amp; Demand Signal Capture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Stock Lookup Analytics &amp; Demand Signal Capture: (a) system captures all stock lookup events (whether reserved or not) as demand signals: (i) items frequently searched but out of stock → potential lost sales, flagged to Category Manager for assortment review (W679); (ii) stores frequently searched for items they don&#x27;t carry → potential assortment gap; (iii) items with high lookup-to-reservation conversion but low reservation-to-purchase conversion → possible store-level fulfillment issues; (b) analytics dashboard updated daily for Category Managers and Supply Planners; (c) data feeds into demand forecasting (W31) as a leading indicator
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1114_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1114_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1114_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1114_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1114_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: POS-level ATP deduction prevents sale of reserved stock to walk-in customers; operational: inventory record accuracy target ≥ 97%
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager (digital channels); Customer Service Representative (phone/in-store)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1114_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1114_Annotation10" targetRef="W1114_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1114_Flow12" sourceRef="W1114_Start4" targetRef="W1114_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1114_Flow13" sourceRef="W1114_Task5" targetRef="W1114_Task6" />
