    <bpmn:process id="W_W1122" name="W1122. Customer Project Material Delivery Photo Documentation &amp; Proof Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Delivery of project materials to a customer&#x27;s construction site or home, especially for B2B/trade accounts and staged deliveries
Frequency: ~8,000–12,000 project deliveries/month requiring photo documentation (primarily B2B/trade, high-value, and staged deliveries)
Volume: 5–15 photos per delivery
Owner: Delivery Driver / Logistics Coordinator
Participants: Delivery Driver, Customer (Site Representative), Logistics Coordinator, Trade Account Manager
Source: workflow W1122 — Customer Project Material Delivery Photo Documentation &amp; Proof Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1122_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1122_Lane1" name="Logistics Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1122_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1122_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1122_Lane2" name="Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1122_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1122_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1122_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1122_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1122_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1122_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1122_Start5" name="Delivery of project materials to a customer&#x27;s construction site or home, especially for…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1122_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1122_Task6" name="Pre-Delivery Preparation &amp; Delivery Order Assignment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Pre-Delivery Preparation &amp; Delivery Order Assignment: (a) Logistics Coordinator assigns delivery to driver with delivery order details: (i) customer name, trade account number (if applicable); (ii) delivery address and site contact person/number; (iii) itemized material list with quantities; (iv) special delivery instructions (e.g., &quot;Enter through gate on south side,&quot; &quot;Unload inside garage,&quot; &quot;Forklift delivery — ensure site has compacted surface&quot;); (v) whether photo documentation is required: mandatory for all B2B/trade deliveries, B2C deliveries &gt; PHP 20,000, and all staged project deliveries; (b) driver reviews delivery order on handheld tablet and plans route
Responsible (R): Logistics Coordinator / Driver
Accountable (A): Logistics Coordinator
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1122_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1122_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1122_Task7" name="On-Site Arrival &amp; Condition Documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: On-Site Arrival &amp; Condition Documentation: (a) upon arrival at delivery site, driver photographs: (i) Site approach photo: truck at the delivery location, showing the site entrance and surrounding area (establishes delivery was made to the correct address); (ii) Unloading area condition photo: the area where materials will be placed, showing pre-existing conditions (existing damage, puddles, obstructions) — this protects BuildRight from claims of property damage; (iii) Material on truck photo: all materials visible on the truck before unloading, establishing the &quot;before&quot; condition of goods in BuildRight&#x27;s custody; (b) photos are timestamped and GPS-tagged by the tablet camera (verifying location and time of arrival); (c) if site conditions are unfavorable (e.g., muddy, no access, no one to receive), driver contacts Logistics Coordinator for instructions before unloading
Responsible (R): Driver
Accountable (A): Logistics Coordinator
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1122_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1122_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1122_Task8" name="Unloading &amp; Material Placement Documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Unloading &amp; Material Placement Documentation: (a) driver unloads materials at the designated location; (b) during/after unloading, driver photographs: (i) Material offloaded — grouped photo: all materials placed at the delivery point, arranged so individual items/quantities are visible; (ii) Close-up of material condition: representative close-ups showing that cement bags are intact, tile boxes are sealed, lumber is undamaged, paint cans are unopened; (iii) Quantity verification photo: for counted items (bags, boxes, bundles), a photo showing the count — e.g., a row of 50 cement bags clearly showing the full count; (iv) Special items photo: any high-value or fragile items (power tools, glass, appliances) photographed individually with serial number visible if applicable; (v) Placement photo: materials in their final resting position, showing proximity to structures and weather protection (if covered/uncovered); (c) all photos automatically uploaded to cloud storage in real-time via driver&#x27;s tablet (4G/LTE connection)
Responsible (R): Driver
Accountable (A): Logistics Coordinator
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1122_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1122_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1122_Task9" name="Customer Sign-Off &amp; Digital POD">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer Sign-Off &amp; Digital POD: (a) customer&#x27;s site representative reviews the delivery: (i) verifies item count matches delivery order; (ii) inspects material condition; (b) if everything is correct: (i) site representative signs digital POD on driver&#x27;s tablet (stylus or finger signature); (ii) system captures signature image, signer name, signer role (foreman, homeowner, site engineer), and timestamp; (iii) system generates digital delivery receipt with: item list, quantities, photos, signature, GPS coordinates, timestamp; (iv) receipt emailed to customer and Trade Account Manager; (v) receipt stored in document management (W255) linked to the delivery order and sales order; (c) if there are discrepancies: (i) driver photographs the discrepancy (e.g., 2 broken tile boxes); (ii) discrepancy noted on POD with quantity short/damaged; (iii) system triggers a shortage/damage investigation per W91 (damaged goods disposition) and W500 (transfer order in-transit damage claim); (iv) driver does not leave until discrepancy is documented and acknowledged by both parties
Responsible (R): Driver / Customer Site Representative
Accountable (A): Logistics Coordinator
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1122_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1122_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1122_Task10" name="Post-Delivery Photo Archive &amp; Analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-Delivery Photo Archive &amp; Analytics: (a) all delivery photos archived in cloud storage: (i) organized by delivery order number, date, and customer account; (ii) retained for 10 years (BIR requirement for transaction documentation); (iii) accessible to: Logistics Coordinator (operations), Trade Account Manager (customer service), Finance (billing dispute resolution), Legal (liability claims); (b) monthly delivery documentation compliance report: (i) % of required deliveries with complete photo documentation (target: ≥ 98%); (ii) common photo quality issues (blurry, missing categories, no GPS tag); (iii) dispute resolution effectiveness: % of delivery disputes resolved using photo evidence vs. requiring further investigation; (iv) average photos per delivery and average file size (for storage planning); (c) photo analytics used for: (i) driver performance scoring (documentation completeness); (ii) site risk assessment (difficult access sites flagged for future delivery planning); (iii) damage trend analysis (specific routes or handling methods causing more damage)
Responsible (R): System / Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): Logistics Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1122_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1122_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1122_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1122_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1122_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: Delivery Driver / Logistics Coordinator review and approval gate
Owner: Delivery Driver / Logistics Coordinator</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1122_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1122_Annotation12" targetRef="W1122_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1122_Flow14" sourceRef="W1122_Start5" targetRef="W1122_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1122_Flow15" sourceRef="W1122_Task6" targetRef="W1122_Task7" />
