    <bpmn:process id="W_W1126" name="W1126. Customer Bulk Cement &amp; Sand Order Direct-to-Site Delivery Tracking" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer places bulk order for cement, sand, gravel, or aggregates requiring direct-to-construction-site delivery
Frequency: ~8,000–10,000 bulk DSD orders/month across all stores (one register with W964: ~40–50/store/month)
Volume: 1–5 deliveries per order; ~50–500 bags of cement or 1–10 cubic meters of sand/gravel per delivery
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate, Receiving Clerk, Delivery Partner (3PL), Customer
Source: workflow W1126 — Customer Bulk Cement &amp; Sand Order Direct-to-Site Delivery Tracking</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1126_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1126_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1126_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1126_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1126_Lane2" name="Supply Chain Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1126_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1126_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1126_Lane3" name="Delivery Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1126_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1126_Lane4" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1126_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1126_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1126_Start6" name="Customer places bulk order for cement, sand, gravel, or aggregates requiring…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1126_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1126_Task7" name="Bulk Order Intake &amp; Delivery Scheduling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Bulk Order Intake &amp; Delivery Scheduling: (a) customer (typically contractor or project account) requests bulk cement/sand/gravel delivery; specifies: delivery address (or GPS coordinates for construction sites), delivery date/time window, quantity (bags of cement, cubic meters of sand/gravel), product specifications (cement brand/grade, sand type — washed, fine, coarse); (b) sales associate enters order in ERP as DSD sales order with delivery scheduling; (c) system validates customer credit limit (W888 credit hold check) for project/trade accounts; (d) delivery fee calculated based on distance from nearest source (vendor depot or quarry) and volume; (e) order confirmed with customer: delivery date, time window (4-hour), driver contact number, and delivery instructions
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1126_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1126_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1126_Task8" name="Vendor/Querry Coordination &amp; Dispatch">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Vendor/Querry Coordination &amp; Dispatch: (a) ERP sends purchase/delivery order to cement vendor or sand/gravel supplier; (b) for BuildRight-managed delivery: 3PL truck dispatched from vendor depot with delivery manifest; (c) for vendor-managed delivery: vendor dispatches directly with BuildRight tracking requirement; (d) system sends delivery confirmation SMS/email to customer with: driver name, plate number, estimated arrival time, delivery quantity, and site contact instructions; (e) GPS tracking activated for BuildRight-managed deliveries via fleet telematics (W199)
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Coordinator (HQ) / 3PL
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1126_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1126_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1126_Task9" name="On-Site Delivery Verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: On-Site Delivery Verification: (a) driver arrives at construction site, contacts customer&#x27;s site representative; (b) for cement: site representative counts bags unloaded against delivery manifest; (c) for sand/gravel: volume verified by truck measurement (standard truck volumes: 1 cu.m., 3 cu.m., 6 cu.m., 10 cu.m.); (d) driver photographs delivery: loaded truck before unloading, unloading process, delivered material on-site, and customer&#x27;s site representative; (e) site representative signs delivery receipt on driver&#x27;s mobile device (digital POD); (f) if short delivery or quality issue: discrepancy noted on digital POD with photos; (g) GPS coordinates and timestamp auto-captured by delivery app
Responsible (R): Delivery Driver / Customer Site Rep
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1126_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1126_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1126_Task10" name="Delivery Confirmation &amp; Invoicing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Delivery Confirmation &amp; Invoicing: (a) delivery app syncs POD data to ERP in near-real-time; (b) system matches delivery quantity to sales order: full delivery → auto-invoice generated and sent to customer; partial delivery → system creates backorder for remaining quantity per W56; (c) for COD customers: payment collected by driver (cash) or via mobile payment (GCash) at delivery; (d) for trade/project accounts: invoice added to account with agreed payment terms; (e) delivery exception (shortage, damage, refusal) triggers customer service follow-up within 4 hours
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1126_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1126_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1126_Task11" name="Monthly DSD Performance Review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly DSD Performance Review: (a) monthly report generated: on-time delivery rate, delivery accuracy (quantity match rate), customer complaint rate, average delivery lead time by region; (b) vendor DSD performance reviewed per W44; (c) 3PL delivery partner performance reviewed per W242; (d) delivery fee accuracy reviewed and adjusted quarterly
Responsible (R): Supply Chain Coordinator (HQ)
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1126_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1126_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1126_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1126_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1126_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials) review and approval gate
