    <bpmn:process id="W_W1131" name="W1131. Customer Construction Project Milestone Photo Documentation &amp; Progress Tracking Portal" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer enrolls project in BuildRight&#x27;s project tracking portal, or project milestone delivery is scheduled
Frequency: ~500–800 active tracked projects at any time; ~2,000–3,000 milestone photo uploads/month
Volume: 3–8 photos per milestone; 5–10 milestones per project
Owner: Sales Associate (Project Liaison)
Participants: Sales Associate (Project Liaison), Customer, Contractor, Delivery Partner
Source: workflow W1131 — Customer Construction Project Milestone Photo Documentation &amp; Progress Tracking Portal</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1131_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1131_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1131_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1131_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1131_Lane2" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1131_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1131_Lane3" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1131_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1131_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1131_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1131_Start5" name="Customer enrolls project in BuildRight&#x27;s project tracking portal, or project milestone…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1131_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1131_Task6" name="Project Enrollment &amp; Portal Setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project Enrollment &amp; Portal Setup: (a) when a trade/project customer places their first project order, Sales Associate offers enrollment in BuildRight&#x27;s Project Tracker; (b) customer creates account on BuildRight mobile app or web portal; (c) project profile created: project name, location, scope (bathroom renovation, house construction, commercial fit-out), estimated timeline, assigned store, project liaison; (d) milestone schedule defined based on project scope: demolition, plumbing rough-in, electrical rough-in, masonry, tiling, painting, fixture installation, final walkthrough; (e) customer grants consent for &quot;Built with BuildRight&quot; photo usage in marketing (opt-in)
Responsible (R): Sales Associate (Project Liaison)
Accountable (A): Customer
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1131_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1131_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1131_Task7" name="Milestone Photo Capture &amp; Upload">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Milestone Photo Capture &amp; Upload: (a) at each material delivery or project milestone, designated party (customer, contractor, or BuildRight delivery driver) photographs progress: overall room/site photo showing work completed, close-up of installed BuildRight materials (tiles, paint, fixtures), before/after comparison at key milestones; (b) photos uploaded to BuildRight Project Tracker via mobile app with timestamp and GPS metadata; (c) system auto-tags photos with relevant project milestone based on delivery schedule; (d) customer can add notes and annotations to photos
Responsible (R): Customer / Contractor / Delivery Driver
Accountable (A): Customer
Duration: 5–10 min per milestone</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1131_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1131_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1131_Task8" name="System-Triggered Next-Phase Recommendation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: System-Triggered Next-Phase Recommendation: (a) when milestone photos show completion of a phase (e.g., tiling complete), system triggers next-phase material recommendation: grout and sealant for tile phase, paint and primer for painting phase, fixtures and accessories for installation phase; (b) notification sent to customer via app: &quot;Your tiling looks great! Next, you&#x27;ll need grout and sealant. [View Recommended Products]&quot;; (c) project liaison reviews notification and follows up with proactive call per W744; (d) system estimates remaining material needs based on project scope and completed milestones
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Sales Associate
Duration: Automated (5 min review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1131_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1131_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1131_Task9" name="Project Completion &amp; Content Curation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Project Completion &amp; Content Curation: (a) when customer marks project complete, system generates project summary: timeline, total material cost, before/after photos, products used; (b) customer invited to write a review per W510 and share project on social media with #BuiltWithBuildRight hashtag; (c) with customer consent, project featured on BuildRight&#x27;s website gallery (W905) and social media; (d) project liaison sends completion congratulations and W914 incentive if applicable; (e) project record archived in customer&#x27;s account for future reorder per W969
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1131_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1131_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1131_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1131_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1131_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: system accepts all uploads and the marketing team curates; operational: consent and privacy review required before marketing use
Owner: Sales Associate (Project Liaison)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1131_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1131_Annotation11" targetRef="W1131_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1131_Flow13" sourceRef="W1131_Start5" targetRef="W1131_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1131_Flow14" sourceRef="W1131_Task6" targetRef="W1131_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1131_Flow15" sourceRef="W1131_Task7" targetRef="W1131_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1131_Flow16" sourceRef="W1131_Task8" targetRef="W1131_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1131_Flow17" sourceRef="W1131_Task9" targetRef="W1131_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
