    <bpmn:process id="W_W1143" name="W1143. Customer Construction Material Pre-Order Reservation &amp; Price Lock Service" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests reservation of construction materials for a future project with guaranteed pricing, or customer presents an approved project quotation requiring material price lock
Frequency: ~1,500–2,500 pre-order reservations/month across all stores (primarily B2B/project accounts)
Volume: 1 reservation per request; average PHP 80,000–500,000 per reservation
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)
Participants: Sales Associate, Department Supervisor, Customer, Supply Chain Planning Team (HQ)
Source: workflow W1143 — Customer Construction Material Pre-Order Reservation &amp; Price Lock Service</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1143_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1143_Lane1" name="Sales Associate">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1143_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1143_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1143_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1143_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1143_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1143_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1143_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1143_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1143_Start4" name="Customer requests reservation of construction materials for a future project with…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1143_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1143_Task5" name="Reservation Request &amp; Price Lock Assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Reservation Request &amp; Price Lock Assessment: (a) customer presents project material list and requests price lock; (b) sales associate verifies customer account status (active, good credit standing, no overdue AR per W888); (c) associate enters material list into ERP reservation module with requested quantities and preferred delivery dates; (d) system checks current inventory and incoming supply for each item across relevant DCs; (e) system calculates total estimated order value at current prices; (f) associate reviews price lock eligibility: cement, rebar, lumber, plywood, roofing, pipes — eligible for 30–90 day lock; electrical, plumbing fixtures, tiles — eligible for 30–60 day lock; promotional and seasonal items — not eligible for price lock
Responsible (R): Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1143_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1143_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1143_Task6" name="Deposit Collection &amp; Reservation Confirmation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Deposit Collection &amp; Reservation Confirmation: (a) customer pays reservation deposit: 10% for trade accounts with credit history, 25% for new or cash accounts; (b) deposit collected via cash, card, or GCash at POS; (c) system creates formal reservation order with unique reservation number; (d) reserved quantities deducted from available-to-promise (ATP) inventory but not from physical stock; (e) price lock expiry date set (30/60/90 days based on material category and customer tier); (f) customer receives reservation confirmation via email/SMS: reserved items, quantities, locked prices, expiry date, deposit amount, and delivery scheduling instructions
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1143_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1143_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1143_Task7" name="Reservation Monitoring &amp; Expiry Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Reservation Monitoring &amp; Expiry Management: (a) system generates daily report of active reservations approaching expiry (7-day warning, 3-day warning, 1-day warning); (b) sales associate contacts customer for reservations within 7 days of expiry: confirm delivery schedule, request extension (one-time 15-day extension permitted with supervisor approval), or convert to order; (c) if customer confirms delivery: reservation converted to sales order with delivery scheduling per W1126; (d) if reservation expires without action: deposit forfeited per terms (deposit refundable minus 5% restocking fee if cancelled within first 7 days, non-refundable after); (e) expired reservation quantities released back to available inventory
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 2–3 min/reservation</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1143_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1143_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1143_Task8" name="Partial Delivery Call-Off &amp; Balance Tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Partial Delivery Call-Off &amp; Balance Tracking: (a) customer calls off partial delivery as project progresses; (b) each call-off creates a delivery order from reservation balance; (c) delivered quantities billed at locked price regardless of current market price; (d) deposit applied proportionally against delivered value (e.g., 10% deposit credited against each delivery invoice); (e) system tracks reservation balance: original quantity, delivered quantity, remaining quantity, remaining deposit; (f) if customer requests additional quantity beyond reservation: additional quantity priced at prevailing rate
Responsible (R): Sales Associate / System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1143_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1143_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1143_Task9" name="Reservation Closure &amp; Deposit Reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Reservation Closure &amp; Deposit Reconciliation: (a) when all reserved quantities delivered, or customer confirms remaining quantities no longer needed, reservation closed; (b) final invoice generated reflecting all deliveries at locked prices; (c) remaining deposit balance applied to final invoice or refunded within 7 business days; (d) system generates reservation performance summary: price saved vs. market (positive if prices rose during lock period, zero/negative if prices fell), fill rate (quantity delivered vs. reserved), delivery timeliness; (e) summary stored in customer account record for future quotation reference
Responsible (R): System / Sales Associate
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1143_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1143_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1143_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1143_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1143_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: management
Owner: Department Supervisor (Lumber &amp; Building Materials)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1143_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1143_Annotation11" targetRef="W1143_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
