    <bpmn:process id="W_W1144" name="W1144. Store-Level Customer Hazardous Material Transport Regulation Advisory" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer purchases hazardous materials (paint, solvents, adhesives, pesticides, LPG, chemicals) requiring transport, or customer inquires about transport regulations
Frequency: ~15,000–20,000 transactions/month involving hazmat items across all stores
Volume: 1–10 hazmat items per transaction
Owner: Sales Associate / Cashier
Participants: Sales Associate, Customer, Delivery Partner (if delivery selected)
Source: workflow W1144 — Store-Level Customer Hazardous Material Transport Regulation Advisory</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1144_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1144_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1144_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1144_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1144_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1144_Lane2" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1144_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1144_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1144_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1144_Start4" name="Customer purchases hazardous materials (paint, solvents, adhesives, pesticides, LPG…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1144_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1144_Task5" name="Hazmat Item Detection at POS">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Hazmat Item Detection at POS: (a) POS system scans item and identifies hazmat classification from item master flag (linked to SDS data per W698); (b) system displays hazmat transport advisory prompt with hazard class: flammable (Class 3), corrosive (Class 8), toxic (Class 6.1), compressed gas (Class 2), oxidizer (Class 5.1); (c) system checks total quantity of hazmat items in transaction against threshold limits for private vehicle transport: paint/thinners ≤ 60L per vehicle (per DOTr guidelines for personal use exemption), LPG ≤ 1 tank per private vehicle, pesticides ≤ 5L per private vehicle; (d) if any item exceeds private transport limit, system flags for delivery recommendation
Responsible (R): System / Cashier
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 15–30 sec</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1144_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1144_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1144_Task6" name="Customer Transport Advisory &amp; Safety Briefing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customer Transport Advisory &amp; Safety Briefing: (a) cashier informs customer of transport advisory: material classification, quantity restrictions, and safe transport recommendations; (b) key safety instructions provided verbally and printed on receipt: &quot;Keep containers upright. Do not expose to direct sunlight. Ensure vehicle ventilation. Do not transport in enclosed passenger compartment.&quot;; (c) for island customers (especially Visayas/Mindanao): &quot;Maritime regulation prohibits carrying flammable liquids, LPG, and toxic substances as passenger baggage on RORO ferries. These items must be declared as cargo and transported in the vehicle hold or via separate cargo booking.&quot;; (d) for items exceeding private transport limits: customer offered BuildRight delivery service (W5D) or 3PL hazmat-certified delivery (W19) with DG-compliant vehicle
Responsible (R): Cashier
Accountable (A): Cashier
Duration: 1–2 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1144_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1144_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1144_Task7" name="Delivery Option Processing (If Required)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Delivery Option Processing (If Required): (a) if customer selects delivery for hazmat items: delivery order created in ERP with DG classification flag; (b) system routes order to DG-certified delivery partner or BuildRight&#x27;s own fleet (if hazmat-equipped); (c) delivery fee includes hazmat handling surcharge (10–15% premium); (d) delivery partner ensures proper DG placarding, segregation (incompatible materials separated), and documentation (dangerous goods declaration if applicable); (e) customer signs DG transport acknowledgment at delivery
Responsible (R): Cashier / Delivery Partner
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1144_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1144_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1144_Task8" name="Compliance Logging &amp; Reporting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Compliance Logging &amp; Reporting: (a) POS logs hazmat advisory delivery with transaction record: items sold, quantities, hazard classes, advisory type given, customer response (self-transport or delivery); (b) monthly compliance report generated: total hazmat transactions, delivery conversion rate, advisory completion rate; (c) data feeds into hazmat regulatory compliance reporting per DENR requirements (W433 SMR/CMR) and internal safety audit (W140); (d) recurring customers who repeatedly self-transport large hazmat quantities flagged for safety follow-up
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Department Supervisor
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1144_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1144_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1144_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1144_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1144_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: (W518)
Owner: Sales Associate / Cashier</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1144_Assoc11" sourceRef="W1144_Annotation10" targetRef="W1144_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
