    <bpmn:process id="W_W1159" name="W1159. Customer Construction Material Price Escalation Protection &amp; Forward Pricing Agreement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Corporate/project customer requests fixed pricing for a multi-month construction project, or bid/tender submission requires price commitment for project duration
Frequency: ~100–200 forward pricing agreements/year (large corporate/project accounts)
Volume: 20–200 SKUs per agreement; agreement value PHP 500,000–50,000,000
Owner: VP for Merchandising
Participants: Category Manager, VP Merchandising, Finance Manager, Customer (Corporate Purchasing), Head of Trade / Account Management
Source: workflow W1159 — Customer Construction Material Price Escalation Protection &amp; Forward Pricing Agreement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1159_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1159_Lane1" name="Category Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1159_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1159_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1159_Lane2" name="Finance Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1159_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1159_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1159_Lane3" name="VP Merchandising">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1159_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1159_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1159_Start5" name="Corporate/project customer requests fixed pricing for a multi-month construction project…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1159_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1159_Task6" name="Forward Pricing Request &amp; Material Scope Definition">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Forward Pricing Request &amp; Material Scope Definition: (a) customer (developer, government agency, or large contractor) submits forward pricing request with project details: project name and location, estimated project duration (months), material list with estimated quantities per month, current market pricing reference, required delivery schedule and locations; (b) Category Manager reviews material scope: which items are eligible for forward pricing (cement, rebar, lumber, plywood, tiles, pipes — commodities with volatile pricing), which are excluded (specialty items, seasonal items, items with less than 10% annual price volatility); (c) preliminary pricing assessment: current BuildRight cost, current market price, historical 12-month price trend, projected price risk (using commodity indices and FX forecasts)
Responsible (R): Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1159_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1159_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1159_Task7" name="Pricing Risk Assessment &amp; Margin Modeling">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Pricing Risk Assessment &amp; Margin Modeling: (a) finance manager performs pricing risk analysis: for each eligible item, calculate maximum expected price increase over project duration using Monte Carlo simulation with inputs from commodity price indices (cement: Philippine Cement Manufacturers Association index, steel: London Metal Exchange, FX: BSP historical volatility); (b) margin modeling: at proposed fixed price, what is BuildRight&#x27;s expected margin if (a) prices remain flat, (b) prices increase by expected amount, (c) prices increase by 2× expected amount (stress scenario); (c) risk mitigation options: BuildRight hedges commodity exposure through forward purchase contracts with own vendors; price escalation cap (e.g., fixed for first 6 months, then capped at 5% increase per quarter); material substitution clause (if specific brand unavailable, equivalent quality substitute at same price); (d) minimum volume commitment required from customer to justify price lock (typically 80% of estimated quantities)
Responsible (R): Finance Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1159_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1159_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1159_Task8" name="Forward Pricing Agreement Negotiation &amp; Execution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Forward Pricing Agreement Negotiation &amp; Execution: (a) Category Manager and VP Merchandising present pricing proposal to customer: fixed price per item for agreement duration, minimum volume commitment, delivery terms and locations, escalation cap (if applicable), material substitution clause, early termination terms, force majeure clause (typhoon, supply chain disruption); (b) negotiation on key terms: customer wants lowest possible fixed price, BuildRight needs margin protection; (c) agreement executed with legal review (W230) and signed by both parties; (d) FPA loaded into ERP: customer account linked to agreement, eligible items with agreed pricing, minimum volume tracking, expiry date, escalation schedule (if any); (e) customer&#x27;s trade account updated: FPA pricing automatically applied to qualifying purchases
Responsible (R): VP Merchandising / Category Manager
Accountable (A): CEO (for agreements &gt; PHP 10M)
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1159_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1159_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1159_Task9" name="Ongoing Monitoring &amp; Margin Tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Ongoing Monitoring &amp; Margin Tracking: (a) monthly FPA margin report: actual cost vs. FPA price per item, cumulative margin impact, volume consumed vs. minimum commitment; (b) if actual costs exceed FPA price (negative margin): margin shortfall tracked and reported to CFO; (c) if customer purchasing below minimum volume commitment: account manager contacts customer for volume catch-up plan; (d) if commodity prices spike &gt;20% above FPA price: force majeure review and potential renegotiation per agreement terms; (e) at agreement expiry: actual margin performance compared to risk model; lessons learned feed into next FPA risk assessment
Responsible (R): Finance Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1159_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1159_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1159_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1159_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1159_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: must handle multiple active FPAs with different pricing, durations, and terms simultaneously
Owner: VP for Merchandising</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1159_Assoc12" sourceRef="W1159_Annotation11" targetRef="W1159_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1159_Flow13" sourceRef="W1159_Start5" targetRef="W1159_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1159_Flow14" sourceRef="W1159_Task6" targetRef="W1159_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1159_Flow15" sourceRef="W1159_Task7" targetRef="W1159_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1159_Flow16" sourceRef="W1159_Task8" targetRef="W1159_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1159_Flow17" sourceRef="W1159_Task9" targetRef="W1159_End10" />
    </bpmn:process>
