    <bpmn:process id="W_W1160" name="W1160. Store-Level DC-to-Store Delivery Inter-Island Ferry Scheduling &amp; Coordination" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: DC replenishment order for a store requiring inter-island ferry crossing, or weekly ferry schedule review, or ferry service disruption alert
Frequency: ~5–10 inter-island ferry shipments/week across the chain (one register with W1164&#x27;s ~30–40 inter-island shipments/month) (stores on islands without bridge access from DC)
Volume: 1–3 trucks per ferry crossing per store
Owner: Supply Chain Logistics Coordinator (HQ)
Participants: Logistics Coordinator, DC Dispatch Team, Truck Driver, Ferry Operator, Store Receiving Clerk
Source: workflow W1160 — Store-Level DC-to-Store Delivery Inter-Island Ferry Scheduling &amp; Coordination</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1160_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1160_Lane1" name="Logistics Coordinator">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1160_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1160_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1160_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1160_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1160_Lane2" name="DC Dispatch">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1160_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1160_Lane3" name="Truck Driver">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1160_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1160_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1160_Start5" name="DC replenishment order for a store requiring inter-island ferry crossing, or weekly ferry…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1160_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1160_Task6" name="Weekly Ferry Schedule Review &amp; Shipment Planning">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Weekly Ferry Schedule Review &amp; Shipment Planning: (a) each Monday, Logistics Coordinator reviews upcoming week&#x27;s inter-island delivery requirements from replenishment orders (W4); (b) coordinator checks ferry operator schedules for required routes: Davao–Cebu (2GO, Trans-Asia), Cebu–Tagbilaran (Oceanjet, Lite Shipping), Cebu–Dumaguete (Oceanjet, Cokaliong), Batangas–Calapan (Starhorse, Besta), Matnog–Allen (Philippine Fast Ferry); (c) maps delivery orders to available sailings: priority orders on earliest sailing, standard orders on scheduled sailing, hazmat orders on cargo-only vessel; (d) confirms ferry bookings for the week: truck plate number, driver name, cargo manifest, estimated crossing time; (e) contingency plan for routes with single daily sailing: if sailing missed, next available option
Responsible (R): Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 3–4 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1160_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1160_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1160_Task7" name="Truck Dispatch &amp; Ferry Check-In">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Truck Dispatch &amp; Ferry Check-In: (a) DC dispatches truck per standard outbound process (W106) with inter-island delivery flag; (b) driver proceeds to ferry terminal and presents: booking confirmation (printed or digital), cargo manifest (listing all items and hazmat classification), vehicle registration, driver&#x27;s license; (c) ferry terminal check-in: vehicle weighed, cargo inspected (spot check for undeclared hazmat), boarding pass issued; (d) driver boards RORO vessel: truck driven onto vehicle deck, driver may stay in vehicle cabin or proceed to passenger deck; (e) system updated with &quot;in transit to ferry&quot; status via fleet telematics (W199)
Responsible (R): DC Dispatch / Truck Driver
Accountable (A): Logistics Coordinator
Duration: 30–60 min at terminal</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1160_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1160_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1160_Task8" name="Crossing Monitoring &amp; Disruption Management">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Crossing Monitoring &amp; Disruption Management: (a) system tracks vessel via AIS (Automatic Identification System) or ferry operator API for estimated arrival time; (b) Logistics Coordinator monitors crossing for disruptions: weather-related delay (PAGASA advisory), port congestion, vessel mechanical issue; (c) if crossing delayed &gt;4 hours: store receiving clerk notified of updated ETA; (d) if crossing cancelled: contingency options — re-route to alternative port (longer drive), reschedule to next sailing (24–48 hour delay), or dispatch from alternative DC if closer to store; (e) disruption communicated to store and supply chain planning team for inventory impact assessment
Responsible (R): Logistics Coordinator / System
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: Ongoing during crossing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1160_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1160_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1160_Task9" name="Port Arrival, Disembarkation &amp; Store Delivery">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Port Arrival, Disembarkation &amp; Store Delivery: (a) vessel arrives at destination port; truck disembarks via RORO ramp; (b) driver proceeds to store (typically 30 min – 3 hours drive from port); (c) system updates to &quot;en route to store&quot; status; (d) goods receipt at store per standard receiving process (W109); (e) any ferry-related damage (water exposure, shifting cargo) documented and claimed per W500 (transfer order in-transit damage); (f) delivery completion confirmed in system with POD
Responsible (R): Truck Driver / Store Receiving Clerk
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 1–4 hours (port to store)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1160_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1160_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1160_Task10" name="Monthly Ferry Performance &amp; Cost Analysis">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Monthly Ferry Performance &amp; Cost Analysis: (a) monthly report: on-time delivery rate for inter-island shipments (target: ≥85%), average crossing delay, cancellation rate, ferry cost per delivery, damage claim rate; (b) ferry operator performance comparison: on-time rate, cost competitiveness, handling quality; (c) route optimization review: are there alternative routes or ferry operators that reduce cost or improve reliability? (d) annual ferry operator contract review and negotiation; (e) inter-island logistics cost benchmarked against total logistics cost (target: inter-island cost ≤15% premium over land-based delivery)
Responsible (R): Logistics Coordinator
Accountable (A): VP Supply Chain
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1160_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1160_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1160_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1160_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1160_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: Supply Chain Logistics Coordinator review and approval gate
Owner: Supply Chain Logistics Coordinator (HQ)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1160_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1160_Annotation12" targetRef="W1160_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
