    <bpmn:process id="W_W1430" name="W1430. Paint Tinting Color Formula Master Management, New Vendor Color Onboarding &amp; Seasonal Formula Library Update" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New paint vendor onboarded per W36; or vendor introduces new color collection (annual); or seasonal color trend update; or paint tinting machine recalibration per W1130 reveals formula drift
Frequency: New vendor onboarding: 2–3 times/year; new color collections: 1–2 times/year per vendor; seasonal formula updates: quarterly; formula corrections: as needed
Volume: ~8 paint vendors (Boysen, Davies, Welcoat, Nippon Paint, etc.); each vendor offers 1,000–3,000 standard colors; total formula library: ~8,000–15,000 color formulas across 200 stores
Owner: Merchandise Planner (Paint Category)
Participants: Merchandise Planner, Category Manager (Paint), Paint Vendor Technical Representative, IT Specialist, Store Department Supervisor (Paint)
Source: workflow W1430 — Paint Tinting Color Formula Master Management, New Vendor Color Onboarding &amp; Seasonal Formula Library Update</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1430_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1430_Lane1" name="Merchandise Planner">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1430_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1430_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1430_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1430_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1430_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1430_Lane2" name="Store Department Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1430_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1430_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1430_Start4" name="New paint vendor onboarded per W36; or vendor introduces new color collection (annual)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1430_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1430_Task5" name="New vendor formula onboarding">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: New vendor formula onboarding: When a new paint vendor is onboarded per W36: (a) Paint Vendor Technical Representative provides: (i) complete color library file (typically Excel or proprietary format) with color codes, color names, base paint required, and tinting formula (mL of each colorant per base size), (ii) machine calibration parameters specific to their paints, (iii) base paint SKU codes for ERP integration, (b) Merchandise Planner converts vendor format to BuildRight&#x27;s standardized formula format: (i) validate each formula: colorant volumes within machine dispensing range, (ii) map vendor color codes to BuildRight SKU system, (iii) load into formula master database, (c) IT Specialist pushes formula update to all 200 store tinting machines via remote deployment
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner / IT Specialist
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 3–5 days/vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1430_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1430_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1430_Task6" name="Annual color collection update">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Annual color collection update: When a vendor releases new color collection (typically annually): (a) Merchandise Planner receives updated color library from vendor, (b) compare new vs. existing: (i) new colors to add (typically 50–200 new colors per collection update), (ii) discontinued colors to flag (do not delete — needed for reorders of existing customer matches), (iii) reformulated colors (vendor changed formula for existing color code — update and note change), (c) load updates into formula master and deploy to stores, (d) Store Department Supervisors (Paint) notified of changes: new color swatches for display rack, discontinued colors to remove from customer-facing swatch books
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 days/vendor/update</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1430_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1430_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1430_Task7" name="Seasonal formula additions">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Seasonal formula additions: Quarterly, Merchandise Planner adds seasonal specialty formulas: (a) trending colors per Philippine interior design forecasts (e.g., earth tones for 2026, pastel accents), (b) Pantone Color of the Year and related palette, (c) custom formulas requested by trade customers (architects/designers) that may have broader appeal, (d) seasonal promotional colors (e.g., Christmas reds/greens for Dec), (e) each new seasonal formula must be tested: mix sample, compare to reference, verify accuracy before deploying to stores
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 1–2 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1430_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1430_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1430_Task8" name="Store-level formula verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Store-level formula verification: (a) during W1130 (paint tinting machine calibration verification), Store Department Supervisor also verifies formula accuracy: (i) mix test colors from each vendor and compare to reference swatches, (ii) flag formulas that produce incorrect color output (possible formula data corruption during transmission), (b) if discrepancy found: (i) Merchandise Planner investigates (formula error vs. machine calibration issue vs. expired colorant), (ii) corrected formula re-deployed to affected stores
Responsible (R): Store Department Supervisor / Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 30 min/store/month (absorbed in W1130)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1430_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1430_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1430_Task9" name="Formula master governance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Formula master governance: (a) Merchandise Planner maintains formula master governance: (i) version control: each formula has a version number and effective date, (ii) audit trail: who added/modified a formula and when, (iii) store deployment tracker: which stores have the latest formula version, (iv) exception report: stores running outdated formula versions (&gt; 30 days behind) — escalate for IT intervention, (b) annual formula master audit: verify all 8,000–15,000 formulas are current, no orphaned or duplicate entries
Responsible (R): Merchandise Planner
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1430_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1430_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1430_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1430_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1430_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-266 (ensure controlled execution — Custom Fabrication &amp; Processing (PA-09.1).) | - operational: standard operating procedures; system-enforced validation rules
Owner: Merchandise Planner (Paint Category)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
